    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/AugsburgUniversity-MinneapolisMN/744000141957954": {
      "title": "Student: Athletics Communications Assistant (Sports Information), 2026-27",
      "description": "Support the Athletic Communications team during home events by helping run live broadcasts, in-game statistics, digital content, and game operations. This is a great role for students interested in sports media, production, journalism, or marketing. Primary Responsibilities \nLive Production Operate broadcast cameras (fixed/roaming), tripods, and intercoms Run the streaming software, graphics, and score bug Monitor audio levels; cue reads/replays; troubleshoot basic A/V issues Game Operations & Stats Operate video board/scoreboard  Enter live stats using NCAA LiveStats/StatCrew; assist with official scoring Verify rosters, pronunciations, positions; distribute box scores and postgame files Digital & Social Capture short-form video and photos for social and highlights Clip and upload key plays; write quick captions/recaps (follow AP style) Web & Media Update event pages/rosters on the athletics website (e.g., SIDEARM) Post final scores, recaps, and notes; assist with basic graphics (Canva/Adobe) Help with media/photographer check-in and credentialing Event Setup & Strike Pre-event setup of cameras, cables, headsets, computers, and signage Post-event tear down; inventory, sanitize, and store equipment Scheduling & Hours Shifts align with home events: weeknights and weekends; occasional holidays Typical shift: 3–5 hours Flexible around classes; training provided. Work-study eligible students welcome. Compensation and Benefits Rate of Pay: $16.45/hour Minnesota Sick and Safe Time Not eligible for health insurance benefits \n\n Students must be currently enrolled at Augsburg and must be work study-eligible. (If you have questions about your work study eligibility, please consult your financial aid award letter, or contact Student Financial Services: studentfinances@augsburg.edu) Dependable, punctual, and professional; able to take direction and follow run-of-show Comfortable with technology; quick learner; attentive to detail under pressure Clear communicator and strong teammate with a customer-service mindset Preferred   Experience with NCAA LiveStats/StatCrew, Daktronics, Production Truck/OBS, or TriCaster Photo/video skills; Adobe Premiere Pro, Photoshop, Illustrator, or Canva Website CMS familiarity (e.g., SIDEARM) Writing/editing (AP style); basic graphic design Commitment to inclusive storytelling and accessibility standards Students must be currently enrolled at Augsburg and must be work study-eligible. (If you have questions about your work study eligibility, please consult your financial aid award letter, or contact Student Financial Services: studentfinances@augsburg.edu) \n\n All student applicants must attach the following for consideration:  Resume Cover Letter (optional) Augsburg University is an Equal Opportunity employer.  We are committed to providing equal employment opportunity to all applicants and employees regardless of their race, creed, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability, military service, protected veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity, transgender status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. \nIf you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact the Human Resources department by phone at  612.330.1058 or email at hr@augsburg.edu.  Human Resources is located at 20 Memorial Hall. \n\n Augsburg University is committed to helping our student explore their vocation. As a University with a calling, we welcome the unique gifts that each of our employees brings to our collective work, and we are committed to supporting our students as they seek to match those gifts with the needs of the University and our larger community.    Student employment with Augsburg is more than a job - it is an opportunity for Augsburg students to gain meaningful work experience in a supportive setting that promotes professional growth, personal accountability, teamwork and collaboration and quality work that lives up to our mission of educating students to be informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, critical thinkers, and responsible leaders.",
