    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/AugsburgUniversity-MinneapolisMN/744000149683313": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Open Rank Professor in Management",
      "description": "The Department of Business Administration and Economics at Augsburg University invites applications for an open rank (Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor) tenure-track faculty position in Management, beginning August 2027. Experience with international business and entrepreneurship is preferred. Appointment at the Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor level will be based on the successful candidate's qualifications, experience, and record of achievement. For full consideration, applications should be received by November 1, 2026. Candidates who have demonstrated success in teaching and serving students from diverse communities are especially urged to apply.  The successful candidate will have opportunities to teach courses in management, including Principles of Management, International Management, Human Resources, Business Strategy, Innovation and Entrepreneurship. The standard course load is six courses per year.  Faculty members are expected to provide engaging undergraduate instruction, maintain regular office hours, advise and mentor students, supervise undergraduate research and capstone projects, participate in curriculum development and assessment, and contribute to departmental and university service. The Department values faculty who integrate real-world applications, undergraduate research, experiential learning, and community engagement into the study of their discipline. Successful candidates should demonstrate a commitment to creating engaging learning experiences that prepare students for graduate study, professional careers, and civic leadership. Faculty are expected to maintain an active program of scholarship appropriate to their rank. Augsburg values scholarship that informs teaching, contributes to the discipline, and creates opportunities for undergraduate students to participate in research, collaborative inquiry, and experiential learning. Faculty members participate in departmental governance, curriculum development, assessment activities, university committees, and professional service while contributing to Augsburg's collaborative academic community. \n\n Minimum Qualifications A Ph.D. (or international equivalent) or terminal degree in Management or a related field is required for this position. Doctoral candidates will be considered if the doctorate will be completed by August, 2027.  Preferred Qualifications Preferred qualifications include, but are not limited to, demonstrated teaching excellence (through materials such as evaluations or teaching portfolios), experience mentoring students, and potential for collaboration and productive scholarship/creative pursuits.   Candidates should demonstrate effectiveness in teaching and professional activities / scholarship which engages undergraduates and stimulates their vocational potential. Post-doctoral/industrial experience, and/or previous college-level teaching experience is preferred.   Successful candidates will have demonstrated abilities in working in an academic community committed to mentoring undergraduates and intentional diversity. Candidates are thus encouraged to highlight skills and experiences that demonstrate intercultural competence. \n\n Compensation and Benefits The compensation range is $90,000 - $110,00, depending on hiring rank and qualifications. Augsburg University offers a competitive and comprehensive benefits program, including:  Medical, dental and vision insurance coverage. Medical plans include Kavira direct care, which provides free or low-cost virtual and in-home primary care appointments and labs A generous 403(b) retirement program with an employer contribution of up to 8% upon eligibility Up to 100% tuition remission for employees, spouses and dependents, and participation in the Tuition Exchange program with colleges and universities throughout the US Employer-paid short-term disability, long-term disability, and life insurance Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for all employees Paid parental leave Application Instructions and Requirements Initial review of applications will begin November 1, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. To apply for this position, please upload the following documents: Curriculum Vitae Cover letter Teaching portfolio, including a teaching statement/philosophy and teaching evaluations (if available) Research statement (1-2 pages)  Copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts. Official transcripts are required at time of hire. As part of the online application process, candidates are asked to provide the name, email address, and nature of professional relationship for three professional references. One of the references must be able to address your teaching or teaching potential. If your application advances in this search, you will be notified prior to Augsburg contacting your references.  If you have questions regarding the position, please contact: Dr. George Dierberger at dierberg@augsburg.edu.     Augsburg University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color, or any other protected class. If you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at phone number: 612-330-1058 or email: hr@augsburg.edu. \n\n Augsburg University  has maintained a strong academic reputation defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies since 1869. A welcoming campus in the heart of Minneapolis, Augsburg offers undergraduate and graduate degrees to nearly 3,200 diverse students. Augsburg’s mission is to educate students to be informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, critical thinkers, and responsible leaders. The Augsburg experience is supported by an engaged community that is committed to intentional diversity in its life and work. An Augsburg education is defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies, guided by the faith and values of the Lutheran church, and shaped by its urban and global settings. Augsburg invites individuals who share our mission and commitment to intentional diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging to join our community. Augsburg encourages BIPOC, LGBTQIA+, individuals with disabilities, women, veterans and those from underrepresented or marginalized backgrounds to apply.",
      "department": "Business & Economics"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/AugsburgUniversity-MinneapolisMN/744000149958109": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Computer Science 2026-27",
      "description": "The Department of Mathematics, Statistics, and Computer Science at Augsburg University invites applications for adjunct faculty positions to teach introductory Computer Science courses. Responsibilities include teaching one or two sections of introductory courses and/or labs in Computer Science such as Introduction to Computer Programming (Python) Introduction to Object-Oriented Programming (Java) Information Security and Assurance Web Applications and Databases \nThis search will establish a “pool” of instructors for potential openings in Spring of 2027. Applications will be accepted through November 30, 2026. Available courses vary by term. Most classes are held during the day, 2-3 days per week. In addition to teaching the class and grading student work, instructors are expected to respond to student questions through email, hold regularly scheduled office hours, reach out to students with course progress information, and communicate regularly with the course coordinator. A course syllabus with calendar, textbook and homework selection, sample activities and exams, and shared office space are typically provided. Most classes are taught in-person on our Minneapolis campus. Each fall or spring semester course requires approximately 12-15 hours/week for 15-16 weeks.  \n Compensation & Benefits \nSubject to the collective bargaining agreement with SEIU, Local 284 $6,100 to $6,475 per undergraduate course* for the 2026-27 academic year Eligible for 2-4% retirement contribution match Tuition discount for employees and dependents Transit pass discount Not eligible for healthcare benefits \n*Course refers to a typical 4-credit undergraduate course that has met minimum enrollment requirements.  Please note that due to employment law and payroll regulations, we can only employ adjunct faculty who reside in Minnesota or Wisconsin. This restriction applies even to courses taught online. \n\n MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Candidates should be committed to student engagement and student success with a diverse group of learners. A Master's in Computer Science or a related field. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:  The ideal candidate will have some experience teaching at the post-secondary level or significant experience teaching at the secondary level. \n\n For full consideration, candidates must submit the following information at the time of application:  Cover letter  Curriculum vita or Resume  Unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts  Your cover letter should  Highlight your experience or interest in teaching at the university level  Identify your general availability during the day and/or evenings; and  Indicate whether you are interested in in-person or synchronous online teaching (or either).  Augsburg is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color, or any other protected class.   Augsburg University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color, or any other protected class. If you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at phone number: 612-330-1058 or email: hr@augsburg.edu. \n\n Augsburg University has maintained a strong academic reputation defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies since 1869. A welcoming campus in the heart of Minneapolis, Augsburg offers undergraduate and graduate degrees to nearly 3,200 diverse students. Augsburg’s mission is to educate students to be informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, critical thinkers, and responsible leaders. The Augsburg experience is supported by an engaged community that is committed to intentional diversity in its life and work. An Augsburg education is defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies, guided by the faith and values of the Lutheran church, and shaped by its urban and global settings. Augsburg invites individuals who share our mission and commitment to intentional diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging to join our community. Augsburg encourages BIPOC, LGBTQIA+, individuals with disabilities, women, veterans and those from underrepresented or marginalized backgrounds to apply.",
      "department": "Mathematics, Statistics, and Computer Science"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/AugsburgUniversity-MinneapolisMN/744000151629047": {
      "title": "Non-Tenure Track, Clinical Assistant Professor, Clinical Psychology (2 positions)",
      "description": "Augsburg University’s APA-accredited Doctor of Psychology (PsyD) program invites applications for two core faculty positions (non-tenure track) to begin in August 2027. Our program trains students using a broad, generalist, practitioner-scholar model. Multicultural training is core to our program and is woven throughout our curriculum and practicum training experiences. Further, our program is dedicated to the values of responsibility, relationship, and rigor. Through these values, we cultivate a vocation that benefits society, promotes well-being, and advances justice. This full-time, in-person program offers small class sizes and a cohesive, egalitarian faculty that holds a wide variety of theoretical orientations and applied research interests. Preferred candidates will be committed to teaching and mentoring in clinical psychology at the graduate level. Responsibilities for this full-time position (11-month appointment) will include teaching, academic advising, supervision of student research, and service to the university. Preferred candidates will also have competence in applied research within the field of clinical psychology. Classes are offered on weekdays, with occasional evening classes. This position will allow the individual to integrate their unique knowledge, skills, and experiences within a program that emphasizes the role of context and multiculturalism in clinical psychology.  All faculty are afforded time for professional practice or scholarship. This time for professional activity aligns with our commitment to integrate clinical practice and/or research with teaching.  \n\n Minimum Qualifications  PhD or PsyD in clinical psychology or a related field by the time the position begins. Competence in applied and/or translational research in psychology Preferred Qualifications  Experience teaching in higher education (particularly graduate education) Experience mentoring doctoral students in clinical work and/or research endeavors Licensed as a psychologist in Minnesota, or a commitment to complete licensure in Minnesota within the first two years of employment. \n\n Compensation and Benefits The salary range for this position is $77,000 - $82,000, annually, depending on hiring rank and qualifications. Augsburg University offers a competitive and comprehensive benefits program, including:  Medical, dental and vision insurance coverage. Medical plans include Kavira direct care, which provides free or low-cost virtual and in-home primary care appointments and labs A generous 403(b) retirement program with an employer contribution of up to 8% upon eligibility Up to 100% tuition remission for employees, spouses and dependents, and participation in the Tuition Exchange program with colleges and universities throughout the US Employer-paid short-term disability, long-term disability, and life insurance Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for all employees Paid parental leave Application Instructions and Requirements Initial review of application materials will begin on October 26th, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. To apply for this position, please upload the following documents: Cover letter: please address how you meet the minimum and preferred qualifications above A statement on your philosophy of teaching Curriculum Vitae Copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts. Official transcripts are required at time of hire. As part of the online application process, candidates are asked to provide the name, email address, and nature of professional relationship for three professional references. One of the references must be able to address your teaching or teaching potential. If your application advances in this search, you will be notified prior to Augsburg contacting your references.  If you have questions regarding the position, please contact: Dr. Christopher Anders at anders@augsburg.edu.    Augsburg University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color, or any other protected class. If you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at phone number: 612-330-1058 or email: hr@augsburg.edu. \n\n Augsburg University  has maintained a strong academic reputation defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies since 1869. A welcoming campus in the heart of Minneapolis, Augsburg offers undergraduate and graduate degrees to nearly 3,200 diverse students. Augsburg’s mission is to educate students to be informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, critical thinkers, and responsible leaders. The Augsburg experience is supported by an engaged community that is committed to intentional diversity in its life and work. An Augsburg education is defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies, guided by the faith and values of the Lutheran church, and shaped by its urban and global settings. Augsburg invites individuals who share our mission and commitment to intentional diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging to join our community. Augsburg encourages BIPOC, LGBTQIA+, individuals with disabilities, women, veterans and those from underrepresented or marginalized backgrounds to apply.",
      "department": "Doctor of Psychology"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/AugsburgUniversity-MinneapolisMN/744000151454491": {
      "title": "Multicultural Life Student Specialist ",
      "description": "Summary of Position  The Multicultural Life Student Specialist supports the Multicultural Life office by working to leverage strategic University relationships to create a network of support and opportunities that further empowers students to fully achieve their academic, interpersonal, and professional goals. Primary Responsibilities Support the leadership and success of student organizations, including but not limited to Augsburg Indigenous Student Association (AISA), in collaboration with Campus Life Develop, implement, and coordinate programs and services that empower students to persist and graduate, develop and strengthen self-advocacy and leadership skills, and contribute to the advancement of the communities of which they are a part.    Establish, maintain, and foster strategic partnerships with key departments, offices, individuals, and community organizations to support success efforts for students. Work collaboratively with campus partners to devise, execute, and assess retention-based programs, policies, and goals for students. Design and conduct presentations across the University community in order to achieve the department and University missions. Gather and analyze data in order to assess the overall needs of students (i.e. to establish learning outcomes for programs and services; to highlight student learning, engagement, and progress; to improve graduation rates; to demonstrate evidence of student needs, etc.).  Rotate service as first-interviewer for reports that come through the Discrimination and Bias Reporting System. Plan, promote, and serve as staff chaperone for programs, retreats, celebrations, etc. within the department necessary. Recruit and select students to receive scholarships designated for students. Co-manage the Oyate Commons University space and student work study employee(s) Additional Responsibilities Serve on University-wide, divisional, and departmental committees as appropriate. Serve as a community liaison through outreach opportunities, networking, recruitment, and mutually beneficial relationships for the University. Manage budget aspects associated with student services. All other duties as apparent or assigned by supervisor(s). Work Environment and Physical Demands Typical work environment is an office. Sedentary work for long periods of time. Regular phone and computer use. Occasional driving; must maintain current driver’s license. Long or irregular hours with occasional travel.  Intense work environment related to working with students facing personal difficulties; will have a heavier workload during the academic year.      \n\n Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree. Three (3) years of professional experience required working with students (may include graduate school assistantships and/or experience equal to three years).  Demonstrated ability to work effectively with individuals from different backgrounds. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities Knowledge of and skill working with a variety of student communities.   Knowledge of identity development frameworks for related training and programming. Ability to effectively establish and maintain cooperative working relationships. Ability to lead, facilitate, and mentor others in individual and group settings Ability to effectively work independently and in a team environment. Knowledge and skills in advising students including the ability to apply good judgment and discretion, demonstrate patience and understanding (especially in confidential, sensitive, and/or crises in accordance with University policies and procedures). Ability to show initiative; organize workflow; manage one or more projects at a time; and handle frequent interruptions.  Ability to be attentive to details, to be accurate, and to be precise. Ability to learn and use a broad range of computer skills, software, and database programs. Preferred Qualifications Advanced education equivalent to a Master’s degree or specialist certification. Two (2) years of professional experience in higher education. Excellent oral and written communication skills. \n\n Application Requirements To be considered for this position please include the following in your application: Resume (required) Compensation & Benefits at Augsburg The compensation range is $53,000 - $60,000, DOQ. Augsburg University offers a competitive and comprehensive total rewards program including:  Medical, dental and vision coverage A generous 403(b) matching program with an employer contributions of up to 8% upon eligibility Up to 100% tuition remission for employees, spouses and dependents, and participation in the Tuition Exchange program with colleges and universities throughout the US Generous paid time-off, including 14 paid holidays, 12 sick days, 2 community service days, and vacation of up to 22 days per year immediately upon hire Employer-paid STD, LTD and life insurance Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for all employees Equal Opportunity Statement Augsburg is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color, or any other protected class.   Augsburg University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color, or any other protected class. If you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at phone number: 612-330-1058 or email: hr@augsburg.edu. \n\n Augsburg University has maintained a strong academic reputation defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies since 1869. A safe and welcoming campus in the heart of Minneapolis, Augsburg offers undergraduate and graduate degrees to nearly 3,200 diverse students. Augsburg’s mission is to educate students to be informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, critical thinkers, and responsible leaders. The Augsburg experience is supported by an engaged community that is committed to intentional diversity in its life and work. An Augsburg education is defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies, guided by the faith and values of the Lutheran church, and shaped by its urban and global settings. Augsburg invites individuals who share our mission and commitment to intentional diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging to join our community.  In particular, Augsburg invites BIPOC, LGBTQIA+, individuals with disabilities, women, veterans and those from underrepresented or marginalized backgrounds are encouraged to apply.",
      "department": "Multicultural Life"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/AugsburgUniversity-MinneapolisMN/744000151039209": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Undergraduate Admissions ",
      "description": "Summary of Position  \nThe Associate Director of Admissions is a key leadership role responsible for driving sustainable growth in recruitment and admission activities. This position oversees the University' undergraduate recruitment and admissions process and provides strategic direction while also focusing on individualized recruitment and relationship management efforts with prospective students. The Associate Director works with first year and transfer student populations, contributing to their success and ensuring a seamless admissions process. \n Primary Responsibilities \n 60% of time spent on direct student/guidance counselor engagement as well as partnership engagement: Cultivate and maintain relationships with division and campus partners.  Maintain differentiated ongoing contact and communication with key high school staff as well as advising staff at community college partners.  Oversee the student admissions process for all first year and transfer students.   Collaborate with admissions and operations teams to establish recruitment and event planning including travel planning and budgeting.   Provide data reporting and analysis to inform strategy and assess team performance and effectiveness. Provide opportunities to meet with students individually to discuss their professional and educational goals while providing information about the student’s program of interest and application/admissions process.   Coordinate with operations/events to plan and deliver successful recruitment and anti-melt events throughout the year.   Conduct recruitment, yield, and anti-melt activities throughout the entire enrollment cycle. In partnership with the Director, work collaboratively with cross-campus constituents, such as faculty, cross-functional teams, key committees, and other administrative or academic departments, to devise and implement effective integrated enrollment efforts. Assist with regular staff meetings and collaborate with other Associate Directors to further develop our Belonging Organizational Structure. 40% of time spent on administrative tasks: Serve as an inclusive thought leader and strategic partner to aid in the design, planning, execution, and launch of continuous efforts to maintain and build upon Augsburg’s competitiveness within primary and secondary market segments. Manages a team of direct reports, providing skill/knowledge training, guidance and support on the team’s work capacities as well as individual belonging and growth. Assist with application review management, effectiveness and final admission decisions. Collaborate with the Operations Team to execute engaging communication flow through all stages of the admissions funnel and for special event promotion.  Contribute to key strategies, such as Augsburg Applies to YOU with a focus on removing barriers to access for graduate education.  Compile key admissions data reports, analyze trends and outcomes, and recommend actions. Collaborate with the Director to identify and implement innovative methods of engaging with prospective students.   Design, manage, and monitor tailored engagement approaches based on student backgrounds and goals. Identify new opportunities to increase interest and enhance yield of admitted applicants. Support professional development efforts.  Perform other duties and projects as assigned. Work Environment and Physical Demands Flexible schedule including evening and weekend hours Typical work environment is an office.  Working at a desk for long periods of time.    Regular phone, computer keyboard, mouse and monitor use.  Repetitive arm and hand motions. Medium physical work - Exerting 20 to 50 pounds of force occasionally, and/or 10 to 25 pounds of force frequently, and/or greater than negligible up to 10 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Including carrying boxes, pushing carts, and moving inventory on shelves. Travel at various events which include standing, talking, and presenting. Travel that includes flying and driving capability.  Emotional intelligence may be needed in order to effectively relate to and work with students and or families from diverse backgrounds, experiences, and occasional strong emotional reactions.  Valid driver's license and willingness to travel (requires occasional overnight, evening and week-end work).  Ability to travel within and outside of the region to recruit students and represent the University. \n\n Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required. Five (5) years of progressively responsible experience in college admissions, enrollment management, and/or comparable professional roles. Strong CRM, analytical, and technical skills. Strong organizational and supervisory skills.  Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree. Ability to reason/analyze and review several options to determine best strategy. A commitment to our Belonging Organizational Structure and to an inclusive workplace. Proven ability to achieve goals, influence others, and meet deadlines. A history of analytics and or marketing achievements. Ability to speak bilingually: Spanish, Somali, Arabic or Hmong. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities Ability to understand and leverage systems, technology, and processes to manage work efficiently. Ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing. Effective time management and the ability to work independently. Evidence of the ability to work with persons from diverse backgrounds. Ability to mentor staff.  Ability to lead/teach. Ability to work effectively in a diverse work environment. Ability to be attentive to details, be accurate, be precise. Ability to work in a team environment; work independently with little supervision. Ability to reason/analyze.  Ability to maintain confidentiality; ability to show initiative. Able to handle frequent interruptions. Ability to demonstrate patience, understanding. Ability to organize workflow and manage one or more projects. \n\n Application Requirements To be considered for this position please include the following in your application: Cover letter (required). Resume (required).  Compensation & Benefits at Augsburg The compensation range is $65,000 - $70,000 annually, DOQ.  Augsburg University offers a competitive and comprehensive total rewards program including: Medical, dental and vision coverage A generous 403(b) matching program with an employer contributions of up to 8% upon eligibility Up to 100% tuition remission for employees, spouses and dependents, and participation in the Tuition Exchange program with colleges and universities throughout the US Generous paid time-off, including 14 paid holidays, 12 sick days, 2 community service days, and vacation of up to 22 days per year immediately upon hire Employer-paid STD, LTD and life insurance Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for all employees Equal Opportunity Statement Augsburg is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color, or any other protected class.   Augsburg University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color, or any other protected class. If you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at phone number: 612-330-1058 or email: hr@augsburg.edu. \n\n Augsburg University has maintained a strong academic reputation defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies since 1869. A welcoming campus in the heart of Minneapolis, Augsburg offers undergraduate and graduate degrees to nearly 3,200 diverse students. Augsburg’s mission is to educate students to be informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, critical thinkers, and responsible leaders. The Augsburg experience is supported by an engaged community that is committed to intentional diversity in its life and work. An Augsburg education is defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies, guided by the faith and values of the Lutheran church, and shaped by its urban and global settings. Augsburg invites individuals who share our mission and commitment to intentional diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging to join our community.  In particular, Augsburg invites BIPOC, LGBTQIA+, individuals with disabilities, women, veterans and those from underrepresented or marginalized backgrounds are encouraged to apply.  Strategic Enrollment Management (SEM) at Augsburg University  The Strategic Enrollment Management (SEM) division includes four uniquely equipped teams: Undergraduate Admissions, Graduate Admissions, SEM Operations, and Financial Aid. The SEM division’s vision is to be a belonging organization that builds deeper relationships, changes systems, and dismantles the access barriers in higher education enrollment management. Our SEM mission is to meet every student where they are with authentic presence, outreach, and engagement. Our nationally recognized Augsburg Applies to You platform supports this mission through direct admissions, success coaching, and academic belonging. We exist to deliver enrollment results, innovation, service, and the essential infrastructure to attract, meet the needs of, and enroll future graduates. We are a key partner in driving sustainable enrollment growth at Augsburg towards the \ngoal of becoming a medium sized university with 5,000 Auggies by 2030.",
      "department": "Admissions/Admissions Operations"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/AugsburgUniversity-MinneapolisMN/744000150755051": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty: American Indian Studies 2026-27",
      "description": "The Department of American Indian Studies at Augsburg University invites applications for adjunct faculty positions to teach undergraduate courses in 2027.  This search will establish a “pool” of instructors for potential openings in Spring of 2027. Applications will be accepted through November 30, 2026. Available courses vary by term. Most classes are held during the day, 2-3 days per week. In addition to teaching the class and grading student work, instructors are expected to respond to student questions through email, hold regularly scheduled office hours, reach out to students with course progress information, and communicate regularly with the course coordinator. A course syllabus with calendar, textbook and homework selection, sample activities and exams, and shared office space are typically provided. Most classes are taught in-person on our Minneapolis campus. Each course requires approximately 12-15 hours/week for 15-16 weeks.  The successful candidate will possess both a high level of intercultural competency and a commitment to inclusive practice and authentic representation. \nThe collective bargaining agreement with SEIU, Local 284 , covers adjunct teaching at Augsburg University. Compensation & Benefits \nSubject to the collective bargaining agreement with SEIU, Local 284 $6,100 to $6,475 per undergraduate course* for the 2026-27 academic year Eligible for 2-4% retirement contribution match Tuition discount for employees and dependents Transit pass discount Not eligible for healthcare benefits *Course refers to a typical 4-credit undergraduate or 3-credit graduate course that has met minimum enrollment requirements. \n*Course refers to a typical 3-credit graduate course that has met minimum enrollment requirements. Please note that due to employment law and payroll regulations, we can only employ adjunct faculty who reside in and work from Minnesota or Wisconsin. This restriction also applies to online courses. \n  \n\n An advanced degree in American Indian Studies (Masters or PhD) or closely related field. Experience as instructor of record (preferred). \n\n For full consideration, candidates must submit the following information at the time of application:  Cover letter  Curriculum vita or Resume  Unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts  Your cover letter should  Highlight your experience or interest in teaching at the university level  Identify your general availability during the day Professional references may be requested at a later date. Among the distinctive features of the University are its deep dedication to civic and community engagement, robust undergraduate research programs, and a strong belief in the integration of liberal arts and professional studies across all programs. The University's commitment to the local neighborhood and the world is enhanced through the work of four signature centers: the Christensen Center for Vocation, the Center for Global Education, the Sabo Center for Citizenship and Learning, and the Strommen Center for Meaningful Work. Augsburg's commitment to diversity is reflected in the student body: for the past four years, students of color comprised nearly 40 percent of the incoming first-year class. With approximately 1,000 students living on campus, Augsburg engages students in a wide range of co-curricular activities, including NCAA Division III intercollegiate athletics. At both undergraduate and graduate levels, students actively engage in international travel and intercultural experiences that broaden their view of the world and deepen their engagement in it. Augsburg's main campus is located in the vibrant Cedar-Riverside neighborhood of Minneapolis, one of the most diverse areas in the Twin Cities. The University of Minnesota West Bank campus and one of the city's largest medical complexes are adjacent to Augsburg; the Mississippi River and the Seven Corners Theatre district are just a few blocks away. In addition to its Minneapolis campus, Augsburg has a vibrant branch campus in Rochester, the fastest growing city in Minnesota and headquarters of the Mayo Health System. In addition to these locations, Augsburg owns and operates international sites in Mexico, Guatemala, and Namibia. Augsburg is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color or any other protected class. Successful candidates will have demonstrated abilities working in an academic community committed to intentional diversity. Candidates are thus encouraged to highlight skills and experiences that demonstrate intercultural competence.  Augsburg University is committed to providing equal employment opportunity to all applicants and employees regardless of their race, color, creed, religion, gender, age, national origin, familial status, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, marital status or public assistance status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. If you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at phone number: 612-330-1058 or email: hr@augsburg.edu. \n  \n\n Augsburg University has maintained a strong academic reputation defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies since 1869. A welcoming campus in the heart of Minneapolis, Augsburg offers undergraduate and graduate degrees to nearly 3,200 diverse students. Augsburg’s mission is to educate students to be informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, critical thinkers, and responsible leaders. The Augsburg experience is supported by an engaged community that is committed to intentional diversity in its life and work. An Augsburg education is defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies, guided by the faith and values of the Lutheran church, and shaped by its urban and global settings. Augsburg invites individuals who share our mission and commitment to intentional diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging to join our community. Augsburg encourages BIPOC, LGBTQIA+, individuals with disabilities, women, veterans and those from underrepresented or marginalized backgrounds to apply.",
      "department": "American Indian Studies"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/AugsburgUniversity-MinneapolisMN/744000150445399": {
      "title": "Student: URGO Office Assistant, 2026-27",
      "description": "URGO is hiring a student to work during the academic year for approximately 5-10 hours per week. Pay Rate: $16.45 per hour \nThis position is not benefits eligible. Duties Reception for URGO office: Welcoming researchers, staff and students, set up advising appts, answer questions Managing email account Sorting/updating electronic documents Writing/submitting A-Mail announcements Writing story profiles for social media, including some video content creation Developing posters/announcements advertising events Maintaining website Assisting with newsletter Assisting with budget entries/paperwork Maintaining office space cleaning/organizing Supporting URGO work via tabling/classroom visits Supplies ordering for research teams Assisting with events planning and facilitation Tracking student research attendance \n\n Open to current Augsburg students. Work study-eligibility is required. Please contact Student Financial Services for questions regarding your financial aid award. Qualifications: Strong writing skills Friendly/accommodating Experience with multiple technologies (Microsoft Office, Google Workspace, various online applications) Versed in social media and willing to work on marketing for the office Attentive to detail Organized Strong communication skills \n\n Application Instructions: All student applicants must attach the following for consideration:  Resume (required) Cover Letter (optional, but strongly encouraged) \n\n Augsburg University is committed to helping our students explore their vocation. As a University with a calling, we welcome the unique gifts that each of our employees brings to our collective work, and we are committed to supporting our students as they seek to match those gifts with the needs of the University and our larger community.    Student employment with Augsburg is more than a job - it is an opportunity for Augsburg students to gain meaningful work experience in a supportive setting that promotes professional growth, personal accountability, teamwork and collaboration and quality work that lives up to our mission of educating students to be informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, critical thinkers, and responsible leaders.   The Office of Undergraduate Research and Graduate Opportunity (URGO) connects students with both new and existing research and scholarship opportunities on campus, across the U.S., and internationally. Each summer over 30 Augsburg students participate in URGO’s 11-week research program on campus, while others pursue research opportunities off campus at institutions such as Harvard, Mayo Clinic, and the University of Minnesota.    URGO provides advising and application assistance for graduate schools, pre-health sciences, and national fellowships.",
      "department": "URGO"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/AugsburgUniversity-MinneapolisMN/744000152457237": {
      "title": "Student: Registrar Records Specialist, 2026-27",
      "description": "Are you an organized problem solver? Do you want to help your fellow students with registration, documentation, and graduation questions? Consider joining our team! The Records Specialist position in the Registrar’s Office is a customer service-driven and detail- oriented administrative position with a friendly team in an office setting. The Registrar’s Office provides services in the areas of registration, records retention, transfer evaluation, graduation, term/curriculum records, class scheduling, grade recording, document imaging, and veteran benefit certification. Our mission is to ensure the integrity of recorded data while providing timely service and communicating information regarding policies and procedures to the Augsburg University community. Consider joining our team and gaining meaningful experience that can be \napplied to many career fields. Job Duties: Triaging phone, e-mail, and in-person inquiries Processing course registrations Processing unofficial transcript requests Processing other forms such as immunization forms and information release forms Filing and scanning electronic incoming documents into appropriate designations Additional clerical duties and projects as needed Work-study eligible students welcome. Compensation and Benefits Rate of Pay: $16.45/hour Minnesota Sick and Safe Time Minnesota Paid Family and Medical Leave Not eligible for health insurance benefits \n  \n\n Required Qualifications: Currently enrolled as a student at Augsburg University and be work-study eligible. Good communication skills Adaptable and open-minded Attention to detail and organizational skills Positive attitude Ability to work independently and collaboratively with a team Respect for student privacy and confidentiality (adherence to FERPA) Preferred Qualifications: Data entry experience Customer service experience Demonstrated experience with database systems Demonstrated office and clerical work experience History of working well both independently and with others Schedule: This position will be scheduled to work 5-10 hours per week. \n\n All student applicants must attach the following for consideration:  Resume Cover Letter (optional) Augsburg University is an Equal Opportunity employer.  We are committed to providing equal employment opportunity to all applicants and employees regardless of their race, creed, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability, military service, protected veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity, transgender status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. \nIf you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact the Human Resources department by phone at  612.330.1058 or email at hr@augsburg.edu.  Human Resources is located at 20 Memorial Hall. \n\n Augsburg University is committed to helping our student explore their vocation. As a University with a calling, we welcome the unique gifts that each of our employees brings to our collective work, and we are committed to supporting our students as they seek to match those gifts with the needs of the University and our larger community.    Student employment with Augsburg is more than a job - it is an opportunity for Augsburg students to gain meaningful work experience in a supportive setting that promotes professional growth, personal accountability, teamwork and collaboration and quality work that lives up to our mission of educating students to be informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, critical thinkers, and responsible leaders.",
      "department": "Registrar"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/AugsburgUniversity-MinneapolisMN/744000152440644": {
      "title": "Weight Room Student Supervisor",
      "description": "The Weight Room Student Supervisor is responsible for the daily oversight of the weight room \nand fitness facility, ensuring a safe, clean, and welcoming environment for all patrons. This role \ninvolves monitoring equipment use, enforcing facility policies, responding to emergencies, and \nproviding basic guidance to patrons on safe workout practices. \n  Key Responsibilities Open and/or close the weight room according to posted hours, including equipment setup and shutdown procedures Monitor patron activity to ensure safe and proper use of free weights, machines, and cardio equipment Check IDs and verify eligibility for facility access per university policy Enforce facility rules and policies Perform regular walkthroughs of the space to identify safety hazards, malfunctioning equipment, or maintenance needs Wipe down and organize equipment throughout shifts; oversee general cleanliness of the facility Respond promptly and appropriately to injuries, accidents, or emergencies, including administering first aid/CPR when certified and contacting emergency services as needed Provide basic guidance to patrons on equipment usage and proper form upon request Report equipment damage, safety concerns, or policy violations to full-time staff Maintain accurate records (e.g., incident reports, attendance logs, equipment checklists) Assist with special events, facility reservations, or program support as needed Compensation and Benefits Rate of Pay: $16.45/hour Minnesota Sick and Safe Time Minnesota Paid Family and Medical Leave Not eligible for health insurance benefits \n  \n\n Required: Currently enrolled as a student at the university  Strong communication and interpersonal skills Ability to stand, walk, and move throughout the facility for the duration of shifts Reliable, punctual, and able to work independently Comfortable enforcing rules and addressing policy violations professionally Current CPR/AED and First Aid certification (or willingness to obtain within a specified timeframe) Work Schedule:  Shifts vary based on facility hours and staffing needs, including early mornings, evenings, and weekends. Typical commitment: 15-20 hours per week. Monday-Thursday: 6pm-9:00pm Friday: 5:00-8:00pm \n\n All student applicants must attach the following for consideration:  Resume Cover Letter (optional) Augsburg University is an Equal Opportunity employer.  We are committed to providing equal employment opportunity to all applicants and employees regardless of their race, creed, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability, military service, protected veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity, transgender status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. \nIf you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact the Human Resources department by phone at  612.330.1058 or email at hr@augsburg.edu.  Human Resources is located at 20 Memorial Hall. \n\n Augsburg University is committed to helping our student explore their vocation. As a University with a calling, we welcome the unique gifts that each of our employees brings to our collective work, and we are committed to supporting our students as they seek to match those gifts with the needs of the University and our larger community.    Student employment with Augsburg is more than a job - it is an opportunity for Augsburg students to gain meaningful work experience in a supportive setting that promotes professional growth, personal accountability, teamwork and collaboration and quality work that lives up to our mission of educating students to be informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, critical thinkers, and responsible leaders.",
      "department": "Athletics - All"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/AugsburgUniversity-MinneapolisMN/744000152253430": {
      "title": "Head Swim Coach (Part-Time, Seasonal) ",
      "description": "This is a temporary, seasonal, part-time position that has an anticipated start date of October 12, 2026 and end date of February 20, 2027. The work schedule is anticipated to be approximately 10–12 hours per week, with hours varying around meets.  Summary of Position  The Head Swim Coach is responsible for planning and administration of the Swim program. The head coach provides vision, leadership and oversight for current student-athletes, prospective students-athletes, alumni, parents and supporters of the program.   Primary Responsibilities Provide instruction and development in swimming skills, team concepts, physical conditioning, and safety for student-athletes in both individual and team settings. Identify talented and academically qualified prospective student-athletes aligned with institutional mission. Foster the holistic development of student-athletes through guidance in personal growth, academic success, and life skills. Demonstrate competitive progress consistent with program and institutional goals. Plan and execute practices and competitions, analyze performance through film, and facilitate team meetings to support development and strategy. Maintain acceptable student-athlete retention rates to the team and/or institution. Oversee program compliance following NCAA, MIAC, and Augsburg University rules and regulations. Commitment to fostering an inclusive team environment. Collaborate with Admissions to support enrollment goals. Additional Responsibilities Oversee budget management, fundraising, travel planning and program organization. Oversee alumni/parent communication and involvement, including organizing events as appropriate. Organize and participate in team community-service event(s). Manage and/or participate in camps and clinics. All other duties as apparent or assigned by supervisor(s).  Work Environment and Physical Demands Work is performed primarily around indoor or outdoor swimming pools, with exposure to high humidity, warm air, and strong chlorine or chemical smells.  Requires evening and weekend work, as well as frequent travel for games, recruiting, and team-related activities. Ability to stand, walk, and move for extended periods during practices, competitions, training sessions, and recruiting events. Ability to demonstrate swimming-specific techniques and drills, and safely use training and coaching equipment as needed. Frequent use of technology for video analysis, recruiting communication, scheduling, and administrative responsibilities. Occasional lifting, carrying, and setup of equipment (typically up to 25–50 pounds). Ability to respond quickly in dynamic and fast-paced environments to ensure student-athlete safety. \n\n Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree. At least three (3) years of coaching and recruiting experience required, preferably at the college level. Valid driver’s license with clean driving record. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree.  At least two (2) years of full-time head coaching experience, preferably at the college level. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities Proven integrity and leadership skills Strong organizational and communication skills Ability to build and strengthen cross-campus relationships  Ability to work effectively and collaboratively in a diverse work environment. Ability to be attentive to details, be accurate, be precise. Ability to lead/teach and mentor others. Ability to work effectively in a team environment; and work independently with little supervision. Ability to reason/analyze; maintain confidentiality; and demonstrate patience, understanding. Ability to show initiative; organize workflow; manage one or more projects; and handle frequent interruptions. Knowledge and adherence to the MIAC Code of Ethics and ability to follow MIAC and NCAA Division III guidelines and regulations, while exhibiting behavior that represents a positive image of the athletic program and the University. \n\n Compensation The compensation for this position is $8,000, paid bi-weekly.  This position is not benefits-eligible. Equal Opportunity Statement Augsburg is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color, or any other protected class.   Augsburg University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color, or any other protected class. If you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at phone number: 612-330-1058 or email: hr@augsburg.edu. \n\n Augsburg University has maintained a strong academic reputation defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies since 1869. A safe and welcoming campus in the heart of Minneapolis, Augsburg offers undergraduate and graduate degrees to nearly 3,200 diverse students. Augsburg’s mission is to educate students to be informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, critical thinkers, and responsible leaders. The Augsburg experience is supported by an engaged community that is committed to intentional diversity in its life and work. An Augsburg education is defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies, guided by the faith and values of the Lutheran church, and shaped by its urban and global settings. Augsburg invites individuals who share our mission and commitment to intentional diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging to join our community.  In particular, Augsburg invites BIPOC, LGBTQIA+, individuals with disabilities, women, veterans and those from underrepresented or marginalized backgrounds are encouraged to apply.",
      "department": "Athletics - All"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/AugsburgUniversity-MinneapolisMN/744000152731180": {
      "title": "Director of Customized Programs, Global Education",
      "description": "Summary of Position  The Director of Customized Programs provides strategic, operational, and programmatic leadership for CGEE’s customized programming portfolio, with sole responsibility for programs serving external partners and shared responsibility for programs serving Augsburg partners. The Director supervises the customized programs team, leads business development and relationship management, collaborates with CGEE’s marketing team to identify new opportunities and expand customized offerings, and oversees portfolio strategy, resource allocation, financial management, and program delivery. Working with external partners, CGEE staff, and consultants, the Director ensures high-quality educational experiences while overseeing select Augsburg programs and contributing to CGEE-wide strategic and financial planning.  Primary Responsibilities Customized Programs Leadership & Portfolio Management Provide strategic and operational leadership for customized programs, ensuring program quality, effective staffing, financial sustainability, and alignment with CGEE and Augsburg priorities. Oversee the customized programs portfolio, team priorities, resource allocation, workflows, and continuous improvement. Business Development & Relationship Management Develop and maintain relationships with colleges, universities, nonprofits, community organizations, and other external partners to strengthen CGEE’s partner network. Collaborate with CGEE Marketing and Recruitment, the CGEE Leadership Team, and the Associate Provost to identify new programs, partnerships, locations, and opportunities for sustainable portfolio growth. Program Design & Development Lead the design and development of customized international programs in collaboration with faculty, partners, CGEE staff, international personnel, and consultants. Translate academic and partner goals into high-quality programs and oversee program structure, scheduling, pricing, implementation, and leader preparation. Supervision & Team Leadership Supervise Program Managers, selected field staff, contractors, and student employees, providing clear expectations, coaching, professional development, and performance management. Monitor team capacity, adjust assignments and resources as needed, and foster accountability, communication, and collaboration across CGEE. Financial Management & Sustainability Develop and manage program budgets, monitor financial performance, forecast revenue and expenses, and provide regular financial reporting. Oversee program pricing and contribute to long-term financial planning, staffing decisions, and sustainable portfolio growth. Operations, Risk Management & Documentation Oversee systems, policies, procedures, MOUs, and documentation supporting program logistics, participant information, travel, and financial operations. Ensure appropriate privacy, confidentiality, safety, and risk-management practices in accordance with CGEE and Augsburg policies and protocols. Strategic Leadership & Institutional Collaboration Serve on CGEE Leadership Team and related committees and contribute to strategic planning, organizational development, budgeting, staffing, and new initiatives. Collaborate with CGEE senior leadership on organizational strategy and the continued growth and development of CGEE’s customized programming model. Additional Responsibilities Participate in or convene ad hoc committees and working groups within CGEE and Augsburg University. Represent CGEE in professional associations, conferences, and other settings as appropriate. Perform other related duties as assigned by the supervisor(s). Work Environment and Physical Demands Primary work environment is an office setting involving prolonged periods of sedentary work and regular use of computers, telephones, and other office technology. May require extended, evening, or weekend hours for program-related events, meetings, travel, or on-call response. Local, national, and international travel may be required for program development or leadership, assistance, evaluation, partnership development, conferences, and other professional responsibilities.   \n\n Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree. Seven (7) years of relevant professional experience in education abroad, study abroad, experiential education, international education, higher education, or a related field, including at least one (1) year of significant supervisory or management responsibility. Demonstrated experience designing and implementing educational customized programs. Demonstrated ability to manage complex projects involving multiple stakeholders, competing priorities, and significant logistical and financial considerations. Strong foundation in experiential education and place-based learning, with the ability to translate academic and organizational goals into effective program design. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in international education, higher education, organizational leadership, or a related field. Proficiency in a second language. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of critical, experiential, and intercultural learning pedagogies. Strong financial management skills, including budget development, forecasting, financial analysis, and program pricing. Strong relationship-management skills, with the ability to cultivate partnerships and sustain long-term partner relationships. Demonstrated ability to develop new programs and assess opportunities for portfolio growth and sustainability. Strong Microsoft Excel and data-analysis skills. Excellent written, verbal, interpersonal, and presentation skills. Strong supervisory, coaching, delegation, and team-development skills. Ability to work collaboratively with individuals and groups representing diverse cultures, identities, institutions, and professional roles. Ability to exercise independent judgment, manage competing priorities, and work effectively within a complex organizational structure. Excellent organizational and project-management skills, attention to detail, and commitment to accuracy and follow-through. Demonstrated initiative, flexibility, problem-solving ability, discretion, and professionalism. \n\n Application Requirements To be considered for this position please include the following in your application: Cover letter (required).  Resume (required).  Compensation and Benefits at Augsburg The compensation range is $70,000 - $78,000 per year, DOQ. Augsburg University offers a competitive and comprehensive total rewards program including:  Medical, dental and vision coverage A generous 403(b) matching program with an employer contributions of up to 8% upon eligibility Up to 100% tuition remission for employees, spouses and dependents, and participation in the Tuition Exchange program with colleges and universities throughout the US Generous paid time-off, including 14 paid holidays, 12 sick days, 2 community service days, and vacation of up to 22 days per year immediately upon hire Employer-paid STD, LTD and life insurance Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for all employees Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Statement Augsburg is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color, or any other protected class.   Augsburg University is committed to providing equal employment opportunity to all applicants and employees regardless of their race, color, creed, religion, gender, age, national origin, familial status, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, marital status or public assistance status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law.  If you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at phone number: 612-330-1058 or email: hr@augsburg.edu. Augsburg University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color, or any other protected class. If you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at phone number: 612-330-1058 or email: hr@augsburg.edu. \n\n Augsburg University has maintained a strong academic reputation defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies since 1869. A safe and welcoming campus in the heart of Minneapolis, Augsburg offers undergraduate and graduate degrees to nearly 3,200 diverse students. Augsburg’s mission is to educate students to be informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, critical thinkers, and responsible leaders. The Augsburg experience is supported by an engaged community that is committed to intentional diversity in its life and work. An Augsburg education is defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies, guided by the faith and values of the Lutheran church, and shaped by its urban and global settings. Augsburg invites individuals who share our mission and commitment to intentional diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging to join our community.  In particular, Augsburg invites BIPOC, LGBTQIA+, individuals with disabilities, women, veterans and those from underrepresented or marginalized backgrounds are encouraged to apply.",
      "department": "CGEE/ISS (Minneapolis)"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/AugsburgUniversity-MinneapolisMN/744000152718699": {
      "title": "Public Safety Manager, Department of Public Safety (DPS)",
      "description": "Summary of Position   The Public Safety Manager is responsible for managing the daily operations and investigations conducted in the Department of Public Safety. Supervises all Public Safety Officers, including monitoring and enforcing policies, practices, and protocols within the Department of Public  Safety. This position coordinates investigative, enforcement, and educational activities with appropriate university officials and city and state agencies. The hours for this position is 12:00 pm - 8:00 pm Monday - Friday. Primary Responsibilities  Supervise and schedule in-house and contracted public safety officers to provide a 24/7 campus presence, responding with urgent purpose to medical emergencies and security concerns. Manage the full lifecycle of staff development, including vetting, initial training, and ongoing certification tracking for officers, contractors, and student workers.  Lead the development of emergency response plans and crowd control strategies while collaborating with city officials (Police/Fire/EMS) for campus-wide events. Oversee the campus incident reporting process, conducting internal investigations and serving as the primary responder for significant issues during shifts. Ensure legal compliance by accurately classifying crimes, maintaining the daily crime log, issuing alerts, and compiling data for the Annual Security Report. Manage and budget for all security infrastructure, including CCTV, card access, radio systems, panic alarms, and the campus-wide keying strategy. Conduct routine security surveys of campus property and oversee audits and maintenance for patrol vehicles, medical supplies, and department equipment. Assist the Dean of Students and Title IX Coordinator on student conduct-related matters. Additional Responsibilities  Serve as the primary authority in the Director’s absence and participate in university committees to guide campus-wide safety and security planning. Develop and maintain collaborative partnerships with university departments, students, and city officials to foster a unified approach to campus safety. Remain on-call for after-hours consultations and immediate response to critical incidents, ensuring leadership coverage during emergencies. Manage daytime dispatch functions, student-led safety programs, and the auditing of specialized inventory such as medical supplies and evidence. \n\n Minimum Qualifications  Bachelor's degree in the related field.  Minimum of (1) years of full-time supervisory experience in a law enforcement, public safety, or security department required.  Minimum of five (5) years of full-time experience in law enforcement, public safety, or security department required.  Valid driver’s license required and must be insurable under the university’s motor vehicle insurance. Meet state background check requirements under the Kari Koskinen Apartment Managers Act and requirements for a  Protective Service Agent in the State of Minnesota.  Preferred Qualifications  Professional experience in public safety or security in a higher education setting.   Successful completion of FEMA courses ICS-100, 200, and 700.   Experience with security systems, including C-Cure 800 security system, Milestone IP video image software, and installation  and maintenance of a variety of cameras, card readers, door hardware, and related technology and devices.  Experience with community policing.  Knowledge, Skills, Abilities  Excellent problem-solving skills, including ability to initiate a prompt and appropriate response, often under stressful  circumstances that impact life, safety, valuable assets, property, and institutional reputation.  Knowledge of legal issues in higher education, including arrest law, search and seizure, criminal law, use of force, Clery Act,  Title IX, and other relevant legal issues. Ability to supervise employees, including setting goals, managing performance, and motivating team members.  Ability to work effectively and collaboratively in a diverse work environment.   Intermediate computer skills, including creating and editing documents, spreadsheets, and basic databases; sending emails and searching the internet for relevant information; creating custom reports; and searching incident report and security  systems.  Ability to write and evaluate incident reports.   Ability to manage video, audio, and other evidence.  Ability to conduct a full range of administrative functions and project management effectively, with solid organizational and communication skills.  Ability to lead, teach, and mentor others.  Ability to work in a team environment, work independently with little or no supervision.   Ability to maintain confidentiality and demonstrate patience and understanding. \n\n Application Requirements To be considered for this position please include the following in your application: Resume (required) Cover letter (required)  Compensation & Benefits at Augsburg The compensation is $70,000 - $75,000, DOQ.  Augsburg University offers a competitive and comprehensive total rewards program including:  Medical, dental and vision coverage A generous 403(b) matching program with an employer contributions of up to 8% upon eligibility Up to 100% tuition remission for employees, spouses and dependents, and participation in the Tuition Exchange program with colleges and universities throughout the US Generous paid time-off, including 14 paid holidays, 12 sick days, 2 community service days, and vacation of up to 22 days per year immediately upon hire Employer-paid STD, LTD and life insurance Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for all employees Equal Opportunity Statement Augsburg is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color, or any other protected class.   Augsburg University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color, or any other protected class. If you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at phone number: 612-330-1058 or email: hr@augsburg.edu. \n\n Augsburg University has maintained a strong academic reputation defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies since 1869. A welcoming campus in the heart of Minneapolis, Augsburg offers undergraduate and graduate degrees to nearly 3,200 diverse students. Augsburg’s mission is to educate students to be informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, critical thinkers, and responsible leaders. The Augsburg experience is supported by an engaged community that is committed to intentional diversity in its life and work. An Augsburg education is defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies, guided by the faith and values of the Lutheran church, and shaped by its urban and global settings. Augsburg invites individuals who share our mission and commitment to intentional diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging to join our community.  In particular, Augsburg invites BIPOC, LGBTQIA+, individuals with disabilities, women, veterans and those from underrepresented or marginalized backgrounds are encouraged to apply.",
      "department": "Public Safety"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/AugsburgUniversity-MinneapolisMN/744000152995457": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty: Theater 2027",
      "description": "The Department of Theater at Augsburg University invites applications for adjunct faculty positions to teach undergraduate courses in 2027.  This search will establish a “pool” of instructors for potential openings in Spring 2027. Spring 2027 Course Opening: THR 271 Black Theater - 2 credit course \nMonday, Wednesday, Friday 2:20 PM - 3:20 PM \nWhat makes a performance a Black play? How does one take control of histories of oppression, problematic and nonexistent representations, hegemonic narratives, and linguistic forms to create a drama that speaks TO and FOR a community? How does one perform Blackness? And who gets to be counted as “black,” anyway? \n \nThese questions are at the heart of this course, and will come up each week as we grapple with new plays, historical periods, and critical voices. The class offers students an introduction to the history of African American theatre, from the nineteenth century to the modern day, with a focus on how playwrights have evolved the dramatic form and claimed control of their identities to speak to Black lives, cultures, and histories.  Available courses vary by term. Most classes are held during the day, 2-3 days per week. In addition to teaching the class and grading student work, instructors are expected to respond to student questions through email, hold regularly scheduled office hours, reach out to students with course progress information, and communicate regularly with the course coordinator. A course syllabus with calendar, textbook and homework selection, sample activities and exams, and shared office space are typically provided. Most classes are taught in-person on our Minneapolis campus. Each course requires approximately 12-15 hours/week for 15-16 weeks.  The successful candidate will possess both a high level of intercultural competency and a commitment to inclusive practice and authentic representation. The collective bargaining agreement with SEIU, Local 284 , covers adjunct teaching at Augsburg University. Compensation & Benefits \nSubject to the collective bargaining agreement with SEIU, Local 284 $6,100 to $6,475 per undergraduate course* for the 2026-27 academic year 2-credit course pay at $3,050-$3,287.50 Eligible for 2-4% retirement contribution match Tuition discount for employees and dependents Transit pass discount Not eligible for healthcare benefits *Course refers to a typical 4-credit undergraduate or 3-credit graduate course that has met minimum enrollment requirements. Please note that due to employment law and payroll regulations, we can only employ adjunct faculty who reside in and work from Minnesota or Wisconsin. This restriction also applies to online courses. \n  \n\n Candidates should be committed to student engagement and student success with a diverse group of learners. \n Minimum Qualifications \nBachelor's degree in theater or professional equivalence. Preferred Qualifications \nTeaching experience in theater at the college level. \n\n For full consideration, candidates must submit the following information at the time of application:  Cover letter  Curriculum vita or Resume  Unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts  Your cover letter should  Highlight your experience or interest in teaching at the university level  Identify your general availability during the day Professional references may be requested at a later date. Among the distinctive features of the University are its deep dedication to civic and community engagement, robust undergraduate research programs, and a strong belief in the integration of liberal arts and professional studies across all programs. The University's commitment to the local neighborhood and the world is enhanced through the work of four signature centers: the Christensen Center for Vocation, the Center for Global Education, the Sabo Center for Citizenship and Learning, and the Strommen Center for Meaningful Work. Augsburg's commitment to diversity is reflected in the student body: for the past four years, students of color comprised nearly 40 percent of the incoming first-year class. With approximately 1,000 students living on campus, Augsburg engages students in a wide range of co-curricular activities, including NCAA Division III intercollegiate athletics. At both undergraduate and graduate levels, students actively engage in international travel and intercultural experiences that broaden their view of the world and deepen their engagement in it. Augsburg's main campus is located in the vibrant Cedar-Riverside neighborhood of Minneapolis, one of the most diverse areas in the Twin Cities. The University of Minnesota West Bank campus and one of the city's largest medical complexes are adjacent to Augsburg; the Mississippi River and the Seven Corners Theatre district are just a few blocks away. In addition to its Minneapolis campus, Augsburg has a vibrant branch campus in Rochester, the fastest growing city in Minnesota and headquarters of the Mayo Health System. In addition to these locations, Augsburg owns and operates international sites in Mexico, Guatemala, and Namibia. Augsburg is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color or any other protected class. Successful candidates will have demonstrated abilities working in an academic community committed to intentional diversity. Candidates are thus encouraged to highlight skills and experiences that demonstrate intercultural competence.  If you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at phone number: 612-330-1058 or email: hr@augsburg.edu. \n  Augsburg University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color, or any other protected class. If you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at phone number: 612-330-1058 or email: hr@augsburg.edu. \n\n Augsburg University has maintained a strong academic reputation defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies since 1869. A welcoming campus in the heart of Minneapolis, Augsburg offers undergraduate and graduate degrees to nearly 3,200 diverse students. Augsburg’s mission is to educate students to be informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, critical thinkers, and responsible leaders. The Augsburg experience is supported by an engaged community that is committed to intentional diversity in its life and work. An Augsburg education is defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies, guided by the faith and values of the Lutheran church, and shaped by its urban and global settings. Augsburg invites individuals who share our mission and commitment to intentional diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging to join our community. Augsburg encourages BIPOC, LGBTQIA+, individuals with disabilities, women, veterans and those from underrepresented or marginalized backgrounds to apply.",
      "department": "Theater"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/AugsburgUniversity-MinneapolisMN/744000153564259": {
      "title": "Student: Campus Kitchen Leader, 2026-27",
      "description": "Coordinate food operations including freezing food, grocery shopping, and organizing supplies. Prepare/serve/deliver meals or groceries at community sites. Organize/support food security efforts via Campus Cupboard food shelf. Collaborate with members of the Environmental Stewardship Intern team on projects. Work with the Campus Kitchens team to plan events. Stay connected with student groups and engage with them around food issues to build. community around food. Coordinate with other Twin Cities organizations for collaborative events and mutual support. Support Food Lab student cooking appointments and workshops. Complete various administrative tasks including data management, social media content, etc. Work-study eligible students welcome. \n  Compensation and Benefits Rate of Pay: $16.45/hour Minnesota Sick and Safe Time Not eligible for health insurance benefits \n  \n\n Students must be currently enrolled at Augsburg and must be work-study eligible. Strong interpersonal skills. Intercultural competency. Strong organizational and time management skills. Ability to juggle multiple projects at the same time. Driver's license preferred. Shifts vary each semester. Some during the day, some in the evenings, some on Saturdays If you have questions about your work-study eligibility, please consult your financial aid award letter or contact Student Financial Services: studentfinances@augsburg.edu \n\n All student applicants must attach the following for consideration:  Resume Cover Letter (optional) Augsburg University is an Equal Opportunity employer.  We are committed to providing equal employment opportunity to all applicants and employees regardless of their race, creed, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability, military service, protected veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity, transgender status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. \nIf you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact the Human Resources department by phone at  612.330.1058 or email at hr@augsburg.edu.  Human Resources is located at 20 Memorial Hall. \n\n Augsburg University is committed to helping our student explore their vocation. As a University with a calling, we welcome the unique gifts that each of our employees brings to our collective work, and we are committed to supporting our students as they seek to match those gifts with the needs of the University and our larger community.    Student employment with Augsburg is more than a job - it is an opportunity for Augsburg students to gain meaningful work experience in a supportive setting that promotes professional growth, personal accountability, teamwork and collaboration and quality work that lives up to our mission of educating students to be informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, critical thinkers, and responsible leaders.",
      "department": "Sabo Center for Democracy and Citizenship"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/AugsburgUniversity-MinneapolisMN/744000153494390": {
      "title": "Admissions Counselor / Senior Admissions Counselor / Assistant Director of Admissions",
      "description": "Augsburg is accepting applications for Admissions Counselor, Senior Admissions Counselor, and Assistant Director positions within our Undergraduate Admissions team. The Hiring Team will review candidates' applications and place qualified candidates into the appropriate position title based on their experience and qualifications. Strategic Enrollment Management (SEM) at Augsburg University  The Strategic Enrollment Management (SEM) division includes four uniquely equipped teams: Undergraduate Admissions, Graduate Admissions, SEM Operations, and Financial Aid. The SEM division’s vision is to be a belonging organization that builds deeper relationships, changes systems, and dismantles the access barriers in higher education enrollment management. Our SEM mission is to meet every student where they are with authentic presence, outreach, and engagement. Our nationally recognized Augsburg Applies to You platform supports this mission through direct admissions, success coaching, and academic belonging. We exist to deliver enrollment results, innovation, service, and the essential infrastructure to attract, meet the needs of, and enroll future graduates. We are a key partner in driving sustainable enrollment growth at Augsburg towards the \ngoal of becoming a medium sized university with 5,000 Auggies by 2030. Summary of Position  The Admissions Counselor, Senior Admissions Counselor, and Assistant Director of Admissions enthusiastically conduct personalized student engagement for all stages of the enrollment decision making journey. They are responsible for developing deeper student coaching relationships informed and measured by data analytics and results. They will manage a recruitment territory with a focus on cultivating meaningful interactions, engage with an assigned community or program partnership, and support an area of strategic priority. This position primarily works with incoming first-year student populations and will occasionally support transfer student recruitment and events. Primary Responsibilities Direct Student Engagement Embrace and maintain knowledge of the University messaging and positioning; people, programs, outcomes, policies, procedures, to authentically articulate the Augsburg student experience. Conduct recruitment, yield, and anti-melt activities throughout the entire enrollment cycle. Conduct student interviews and presentations (on and off campus).  Visit high schools, organizations, and colleges to present and advise students. Conduct routine cultivation outreach and response (phone, text, social media, email). Conduct virtual recruitment activities i.e. online events, chat, social media, video. Evaluate admission applications. Help plan, organize, and execute engaging on-campus (and off-campus) recruiting events. Utilize Customer Relationship Management (CRM) databases to manage communications/follow up and your capacity accountability. Build relationships with school counselors and other community partners to support students in their college search and application process.   Administrative Tasks Develop and manage a recruitment territory of inquiries and admitted students for each cycle. Analyze recruitment data and use information to determine travel and communication plans.  Responsibility for an assigned area of strategic priority or initiative utilizing the objective and key results framework (OKR).  Additional Responsibilities Serve on cross functional teams that impact the recruitment and retention of students. Successfully complete Augsburg Diversity Certificate program, and Edify DEIB Posture statement.  Attend regular staff meetings and trainings and stay informed of institutional changes that would impact the students' experience. Share trends on what you are hearing from students with the wider team.   Provide input on recruitment strategies. i.e. the Augsburg Applies 2U/Power of US initiatives. Complete routine reports related to recruitment, projections, travel, and special programs.  Work with the rest of the admissions staff to develop the quarterly/annual recruitment plans. Serve as a student success coaching role for prospective students as part of Augsburg Applies to You program.  Extend your prospective student coaching role into working with a limited group of enrolled students to strengthen your recruitment impact related to firsthand knowledge of actual student experiences. Other duties and projects as apparent or assigned by supervisor(s). Work Environment & Physical Demands Flexible schedule including evening and weekend hours. Typical work environment is an office. Sedentary work for long periods of time.    Travel to events, which includes talking and presenting. Regular computer and phone use. Travel that includes flying and driving capability.  Emotional intelligence may be needed in order to effectively relate to and work with students and or families from diverse backgrounds, experiences, and occasional strong emotional reactions. \n\n Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree. Enthusiasm and passion for empowering others to succeed. Excellent oral/public presentation and written communication skills. Technology experience with Microsoft Suite (i.e. Word and/or Excel). Preferred Qualifications Admissions experience as a professional staff member, student employee, or internship. Ability to speak bilingually: Spanish, Somali, Arabic, or Hmong. Effective time management and the ability to work independently. Team player, effective at collaboration. Proven ability to achieve goals, influence others, and meet deadlines. Ability to think strategically, creatively and innovatively on how to recruit and connect with prospective students now and in future admissions cycles. Command of University messaging and positioning; people, programs, outcomes, policies, procedures, to authentically articulate the Augsburg student experience. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Evidence of the ability to work with persons from diverse backgrounds.  Commitment to the SEM division’s mission, vision and values.  Ability to reason/analyze and review several options to determine best strategy. A commitment to the Belonging Organizational Structure within the division, and to an inclusive workplace. Proven ability to achieve goals, influence others, and meet deadlines. A history of analytics and or marketing achievements. Exceptional oral and written communication skills. Excellent presentation and public-speaking skills Effective time management and the ability to work independently. Ability to understand and leverage systems, technology, and processes to manage work efficiently. Strong organizational and supervisory skills.  Emotional intelligence may be needed in order to effectively relate to and work with students and or families from diverse backgrounds, experiences, and occasional strong emotional reactions. \n\n Application Requirements To be considered for this position please include the following in your application: Resume (required) Compensation & Benefits at Augsburg Below is the compensation range for Admissions Counselor, Senior Admission Counselor & Assistant Director.  Admissions Counselor: $21.00 - $21.60 per hour, DOQ Senior Admissions Counselor: $21.60 - $23.00 per hour, DOQ. Assistant Director: $48,000 - $55,000 per year, DOQ. Augsburg University offers a competitive and comprehensive total rewards program including: Medical, dental and vision coverage A generous 403(b) matching program with an employer contributions of up to 8% upon eligibility Up to 100% tuition remission for employees, spouses and dependents, and participation in the Tuition Exchange program with colleges and universities throughout the US Generous paid time-off, including 14 paid holidays, 12 sick days, 2 community service days, and vacation of up to 22 days per year immediately upon hire Employer-paid STD, LTD and life insurance Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for all employees Equal Opportunity Statement Augsburg is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color, or any other protected class.   Augsburg University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color, or any other protected class. If you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at phone number: 612-330-1058 or email: hr@augsburg.edu. \n\n Augsburg University has maintained a strong academic reputation defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies since 1869. A welcoming campus in the heart of Minneapolis, Augsburg offers undergraduate and graduate degrees to nearly 3,200 diverse students. Augsburg’s mission is to educate students to be informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, critical thinkers, and responsible leaders. The Augsburg experience is supported by an engaged community that is committed to intentional diversity in its life and work. An Augsburg education is defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies, guided by the faith and values of the Lutheran church, and shaped by its urban and global settings. Augsburg invites individuals who share our mission and commitment to intentional diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging to join our community.  In particular, Augsburg invites BIPOC, LGBTQIA+, individuals with disabilities, women, veterans and those from underrepresented or marginalized backgrounds are encouraged to apply.",
      "department": "Admissions/Admissions Operations"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/AugsburgUniversity-MinneapolisMN/744000154737825": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty: Physician Associate Studies 2027",
      "description": "The Department of Physician Associate Studies at Augsburg University invites applications for adjunct faculty positions to teach Graduate courses in 2027.  This search will establish a “pool” of instructors for potential openings in Spring of 2027.  Responsibilities include teaching students through small group facilitation, including courses in Anatomy, History and Physical Examination, and Clinical Practice Seminar. In addition, the PA department may have opportunities for clinical instructors in hospital or clinic-based settings.  Available courses vary by term. Most classes are held during the day, 2-3 days per week. In addition to teaching the class and grading student work, instructors are expected to respond to student questions through email, hold regularly scheduled office hours, reach out to students with course progress information, and communicate regularly with the course coordinator. A course syllabus with calendar, textbook and homework selection, sample activities and exams, and shared office space are typically provided. Most classes are taught in-person on our Minneapolis campus. Each course requires approximately 12-15 hours/week for 15-16 weeks.  The successful candidate will possess both a high level of intercultural competency and a commitment to inclusive practice and authentic representation. The collective bargaining agreement with SEIU, Local 284 , covers adjunct teaching at Augsburg University. Compensation & Benefits Subject to the collective bargaining agreement with SEIU, Local 284 $7,100 - $7,275 per graduate course* for the 2026-27 academic year Eligible for 2-4% retirement contribution match Tuition discount for employees and dependents Transit pass discount Not eligible for healthcare benefits *Course refers to a typical 3-credit graduate course that has met minimum enrollment requirements. Please note that due to employment law and payroll regulations, we can only employ adjunct faculty who reside in and work from Minnesota or Wisconsin. This restriction also applies to online courses. \n  \n\n MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:  Physician Assistant Certification (NCCPA) Licensed or eligible for PA licensure in the state of Minnesota Master’s Degree in PA, education, or related field PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:  Teaching experience in online, hybrid, and/or in-person formats. Doctoral degree in healthcare, education, or related field \n\n For full consideration, candidates must submit the following information at the time of application:  Cover letter  Curriculum vita or Resume  Unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts  Your cover letter should  Highlight your experience or interest in teaching at the university level  Identify your general availability during the day Professional references may be requested at a later date. Among the distinctive features of the University are its deep dedication to civic and community engagement, robust undergraduate research programs, and a strong belief in the integration of liberal arts and professional studies across all programs. The University's commitment to the local neighborhood and the world is enhanced through the work of four signature centers: the Christensen Center for Vocation, the Center for Global Education, the Sabo Center for Citizenship and Learning, and the Strommen Center for Meaningful Work. Augsburg's commitment to diversity is reflected in the student body: for the past four years, students of color comprised nearly 40 percent of the incoming first-year class. With approximately 1,000 students living on campus, Augsburg engages students in a wide range of co-curricular activities, including NCAA Division III intercollegiate athletics. At both undergraduate and graduate levels, students actively engage in international travel and intercultural experiences that broaden their view of the world and deepen their engagement in it. Augsburg's main campus is located in the vibrant Cedar-Riverside neighborhood of Minneapolis, one of the most diverse areas in the Twin Cities. The University of Minnesota West Bank campus and one of the city's largest medical complexes are adjacent to Augsburg; the Mississippi River and the Seven Corners Theatre district are just a few blocks away. In addition to its Minneapolis campus, Augsburg has a vibrant branch campus in Rochester, the fastest growing city in Minnesota and headquarters of the Mayo Health System. In addition to these locations, Augsburg owns and operates international sites in Mexico, Guatemala, and Namibia. Augsburg is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color or any other protected class. Successful candidates will have demonstrated abilities working in an academic community committed to intentional diversity. Candidates are thus encouraged to highlight skills and experiences that demonstrate intercultural competence.  If you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at phone number: 612-330-1058 or email: hr@augsburg.edu. Augsburg University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color, or any other protected class. If you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at phone number: 612-330-1058 or email: hr@augsburg.edu. \n\n Augsburg University has maintained a strong academic reputation defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies since 1869. A welcoming campus in the heart of Minneapolis, Augsburg offers undergraduate and graduate degrees to nearly 3,200 diverse students. Augsburg’s mission is to educate students to be informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, critical thinkers, and responsible leaders. The Augsburg experience is supported by an engaged community that is committed to intentional diversity in its life and work. An Augsburg education is defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies, guided by the faith and values of the Lutheran church, and shaped by its urban and global settings. Augsburg invites individuals who share our mission and commitment to intentional diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging to join our community. Augsburg encourages BIPOC, LGBTQIA+, individuals with disabilities, women, veterans and those from underrepresented or marginalized backgrounds to apply.",
      "department": "Master of Physician Assistant Studies"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/AugsburgUniversity-MinneapolisMN/744000154719699": {
      "title": "Student: Campus Life Administrative Assistant 2026-27",
      "description": "The Student Administrative Assistant position provides essential programmatic support to \nCampus Life for its events throughout the year. It also allows the office to maintain a basic level \nof functioning in maintaining consistent communications with the broader campus and greater \ncommunity, as well as providing consistent and reliable services to students and student \norganizations. \nStudent Administrative Assistants are responsible for: Staffing the Christensen Center Student Lounge in addition to checking out Campus Life equipment to students, staff, and faculty, and maintaining the general upkeep of the lounge. Encouraging the respectful and proper use of Student Lounge furniture and enforcing the Student Lounge policies. Performing and implementing administrative and programmatic duties for Campus Life, including answering and returning emails and customer relations. Coordinating and administering student organization and Act Six Scholarship programming, including Student Leadership Institute, and Student Leadership Awards, Student Involvement Fairs (fall and spring). Work-study eligible students welcome. Compensation and Benefits Rate of Pay: $16.45/hour Minnesota Sick and Safe Time Minnesota Paid Family and Medical Leave Not eligible for health insurance benefits \n\n Enrolled or in the process of enrolling at Augsburg University Must have FAFSA completed or waived if eligible for student employment otherwise. Work-study as part of your financial aid award. If you have questions, please contact studentfinances@augsburg.edu Have a 2.0 cumulative and previous semester grade point average. \n\n All student applicants must attach the following for consideration:  Resume Cover Letter (optional) Augsburg University is an Equal Opportunity employer.  We are committed to providing equal employment opportunity to all applicants and employees regardless of their race, creed, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability, military service, protected veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity, transgender status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. \nIf you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact the Human Resources department by phone at  612.330.1058 or email at hr@augsburg.edu.  Human Resources is located at 20 Memorial Hall. \n\n Augsburg University is committed to helping our student explore their vocation. As a University with a calling, we welcome the unique gifts that each of our employees brings to our collective work, and we are committed to supporting our students as they seek to match those gifts with the needs of the University and our larger community.    Student employment with Augsburg is more than a job - it is an opportunity for Augsburg students to gain meaningful work experience in a supportive setting that promotes professional growth, personal accountability, teamwork and collaboration and quality work that lives up to our mission of educating students to be informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, critical thinkers, and responsible leaders.",
      "department": "Campus Life"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/AugsburgUniversity-MinneapolisMN/744000154189519": {
      "title": "1st Shift Custodian ",
      "description": "This position is responsible for cleaning and servicing designated areas according to the established procedures, area of responsibility and other assignments necessary to perform as assigned by the supervisor or lead.  Follow proper cleaning methods, utilizing equipment for each situation, based on training, to ensure the campus maintains a healthy, safe, and sanitary environment. Available Shift: Monday - Friday, 5:00 a.m. - 1:30 p.m. (Full-Time) Primary Responsibilities:  General cleaning of area(s) of responsibility including waste removal, vacuuming, carpet cleaning, detail cleaning of restrooms, entries, common areas, wall washing, Kivac as needed, spot cleaning walls, staircases, dust mop, and mop or auto scrub floors. Detailing area(s) which will include dusting, edge vacuuming, cleaning light fixtures, cleaning and polishing drinking fountains, and straightening furniture and accessories. Buffing floors, Cleaning Carpets, and deep cleaning restrooms as needed. Clean all glass entry doors, inside and out. throughout the shift, as needed. Assist in the coverage of open areas due to vacations, sick calls, and open positions. Additional Examples of Work Performed:  Completing work orders. Clean and maintain all custodial equipment and closets according to set standards. Clean outside entryways, up to 15 feet from the door, and keep them free of debris and snow. Summer and school break apartment turn cleaning. Report damages, acts of vandalism, and needed repairs. Bio-hazard clean-up. Assist with event cleanup. All other duties are assigned by the Facilities Operation Manager, Custodial Supervisor, or Lead Custodian. Work Environment and Physical Demands: Continuous standing, walking, lifting, bending, stretching, kneeling, and squatting.  Exposure to irritating substances: cleaning supplies, etc. Long or irregular hours: may work days, nights, and weekends. Exposure to dust, dirt, mold, dampness, and odors. \n\n Minimum Qualifications High school graduate or GED and one (1) year of experience required. Must be able to read, write and follow directions and/or oral instructions in English required. Physical requirements: Ability to lift up to 40 pounds required.  \n\n Compensation & Benefits at Augsburg The compensation is $22.06 hourly.  Augsburg University offers a competitive and comprehensive total rewards program including: Medical, dental and vision coverage A generous 403(b) matching program with an employer contributions of up to 8% upon eligibility Up to 100% tuition remission for employees, spouses and dependents, and participation in the Tuition Exchange program with colleges and universities throughout the US Generous paid time-off, including 14 paid holidays, 12 sick days, 2 community service days, and vacation of up to 22 days per year immediately upon hire Employer-paid STD, LTD and life insurance Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for all employees Equal Opportunity Statement Augsburg is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color, or any other protected class.   Augsburg University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color, or any other protected class. If you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at phone number: 612-330-1058 or email: hr@augsburg.edu. \n\n Augsburg University has maintained a strong academic reputation defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies since 1869. A welcoming campus in the heart of Minneapolis, Augsburg offers undergraduate and graduate degrees to nearly 3,200 diverse students. Augsburg’s mission is to educate students to be informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, critical thinkers, and responsible leaders. The Augsburg experience is supported by an engaged community that is committed to intentional diversity in its life and work. An Augsburg education is defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies, guided by the faith and values of the Lutheran church, and shaped by its urban and global settings. Augsburg invites individuals who share our mission and commitment to intentional diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging to join our community.  In particular, Augsburg invites BIPOC, LGBTQIA+, individuals with disabilities, women, veterans and those from underrepresented or marginalized backgrounds are encouraged to apply.",
      "department": "Custodial Services"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/AugsburgUniversity-MinneapolisMN/744000153851624": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Corporate Partnerships",
      "description": "Summary of Position Provide leadership for the University in securing external funds to support institutional mission, functions and strategic priorities. Responsible for identifying, planning, facilitating, composing and managing proposals for academic programs, research, sponsored programs, capital projects and sponsorship requests through corporate and foundation relationships. This person is responsible for maintaining internal and external relationships in efforts to facilitate and enhance this work. Primary Responsibilities Institutional Partnerships Identify, cultivate, and solicit funds from local and national corporations and foundations Secure sponsorships and grants to achieve annual fundraising goals.  Work closely with the Senior Director of Grants and Sponsored Programs, the Associate Vice President and Vice President for Institutional Advancement to map and implement an integrated institutional giving program. Develop and execute an annual solicitation plan for a portfolio of external funders; schedule and solicit portfolio through written proposals, personal contact and other correspondence. Identify and implement giving program strategies in order to broaden and deepen institutional support. Work with other departments to invite program officers and other representatives from government and foundation sources to relevant University events and programs. Act as University liaison with institutional donors, including local, state and national funders, corporations and foundations. Manage solicitations with major institutional donors. Represent Augsburg at meetings with external partners and stakeholders as required to plan, implement and evaluate inter-departmental grant-funded projects.  Utilize the President, Board of Regents and other key partners to make connections for the University. Administration Conduct research, follow up on leads and coordinate solicitation of prospects for new support. Read reporting requirements and write/edit interim and final reports to external funders. Support colleagues and board members on annual fund solicitations. Track information about institutional donors and relationships, generating institutional giving status reports. Develop and maintain an archive containing proposal materials and University data. Analyze and track current contribution sources to cultivate and solicit funds. Utilize Raisers Edge to track progress and prospects as well as write and maintain contact reports. Additional Responsibilities Serve on institutional leadership groups, task forces, and committees as assigned. Develop and maintain positive working relationships with the internal and external University community. Other duties as assigned in line with the goals of the division and the mission of the institution.     Work Environment and Physical Demands Typical work environment is an office, working at a desk for long periods of time. Regular phone and computer use. Occasional long or irregular hours, including occasional evening and weekend hours. Some travel as needed. \n\n Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in related field. Minimum of five (5) years experience in institutional fundraising; identifying donors, managing and developing relationships. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree preferred. Professional experience in higher education.  Familiarity with the Advancement databases; preferably Raisers Edge.  Knowledge, Skills, Abilities Excellent communication, organizational and interpersonal skills. Strong analytical and critical thinking skills, attention to detail and accuracy. Strong project management skills with the ability to effectively multi-task and prioritize. Knowledge of direct mail, basic event management, non-profit finance and development principles and practices. Proficiency in Microsoft Office® suite (Word, Excel, Outlook) and Google Workspace suite (Docs, Sheets, Drive, etc). Ability to exercise professional courtesy and discretion, maintaining confidentiality and privacy. \n\n Compensation and Benefits at Augsburg The compensation range is $80,000 - $86,000 per year, DOQ. Augsburg University offers a competitive and comprehensive total rewards program including:  Medical, dental and vision coverage A generous 403(b) matching program with an employer contributions of up to 8% upon eligibility Up to 100% tuition remission for employees, spouses and dependents, and participation in the Tuition Exchange program with colleges and universities throughout the US Generous paid time-off, including 14 paid holidays, 12 sick days, 2 community service days, and vacation of up to 22 days per year immediately upon hire Employer-paid STD, LTD and life insurance Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for all employees Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Statement Augsburg is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color, or any other protected class.   Augsburg University is committed to providing equal employment opportunity to all applicants and employees regardless of their race, color, creed, religion, gender, age, national origin, familial status, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, marital status or public assistance status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law.  If you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at phone number: 612-330-1058 or email: hr@augsburg.edu. Augsburg University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color, or any other protected class. If you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at phone number: 612-330-1058 or email: hr@augsburg.edu. \n\n Augsburg University has maintained a strong academic reputation defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies since 1869. A safe and welcoming campus in the heart of Minneapolis, Augsburg offers undergraduate and graduate degrees to nearly 3,200 diverse students. Augsburg’s mission is to educate students to be informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, critical thinkers, and responsible leaders. The Augsburg experience is supported by an engaged community that is committed to intentional diversity in its life and work. An Augsburg education is defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies, guided by the faith and values of the Lutheran church, and shaped by its urban and global settings. Augsburg invites individuals who share our mission and commitment to intentional diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging to join our community.  In particular, Augsburg invites BIPOC, LGBTQIA+, individuals with disabilities, women, veterans and those from underrepresented or marginalized backgrounds are encouraged to apply.",
      "department": "Advancement Services"
