    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/AugsburgUniversity-MinneapolisMN/744000155851309": {
      "title": "Payroll, Benefits and Leaves Manager",
      "description": "Summary of Position   The Payroll, Benefits, and Leaves Manager manages end-to-end payroll processing, employee benefits administration, and leave-of-absence programs while ensuring compliance with federal and state regulations. This position balances daily operational responsibilities with a proactive approach to accuracy and data integrity. In collaboration with internal and external partners, this role proactively anticipates risks, optimizes technology and workflows, and resolves systemic problems before they impact employees.   Primary Responsibilities Manages end-to-end bi-weekly payroll processes in Workday for faculty, staff, and student workers to ensure accurate and timely compensation. Oversees payroll tax operations in collaboration with the university’s third-party tax provider, securing accurate bi-weekly, quarterly, and year-end reporting and tax filings. Manages statutory and voluntary deductions, tracking specific adjustments for retirement plans, student worker tax exemptions, and court-ordered garnishments. Administers, reconciles and audits comprehensive benefits programs, managing employee enrollments and deductions for medical, dental, vision, retirement, life, and disability plans.  Oversees the administration of Flexible Spending Accounts (FSAs), Health Savings Accounts (HSAs) and COBRA compliance, working closely with third-party administrators (TPAs) to ensure accurate tracking, timely notifications, and regulatory compliance. Leads annual open enrollment planning and execution and processes mid-year qualifying events. Serves as the internal resource for employees with basic questions regarding their benefits, and a referral source to benefits providers for complex questions and cases.  Leads and/or supports the University’s annual retirement plan audit process. Working closely with third-party administrators (TPAs), manages and tracks leaves of absences including short-term/long-term disability, workers' compensation, military leave, FMLA, and state-specific programs (such as Minnesota Paid Leave and Earned Sick and Safe Time - ESST). Manages leave accruals, pay continuation, and benefit premium deductions while employees are on leave. Coordinates leave workflows by guiding employees through the application process and managing the operational relationship with the university’s third-party leave administrator. Remains up-to-date on all federal and state laws and regulations regarding payroll and payroll taxes, benefits and leaves. Critically analyzes gaps and develops reviews and audits to proactively catch and resolve critical issues Additional Responsibilities Maintains Workday system integrity by regularly auditing employee changes, timekeeping records, and student worker status updates. Participates in department and University-wide initiatives and committees All other duties as apparent or assigned by supervisor(s). Work Environment and Physical Demands The typical working environment is an office setting. Sedentary work for long periods of time. This position works on-campus Monday - Friday during daytime hours, with some remote work opportunities after the onboarding period is complete. Frequent computer, video meeting/in-person meetings, and phone work. \n\n Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree and five (5) or more years of directly related payroll and benefits/leave administration; an equivalent level of education/certification and directly-related experience may be considered. Demonstrated knowledge and understanding of payroll tax regulations and applications at the federal and state levels.   Advanced knowledge of employee benefit rules and regulations including but not limited to health and welfare plans, 403(b) or other retirement plans, and ERISA-related benefits. Demonstrated ability to establish priorities and meet deadlines while managing competing demands. Excellent computer skills and ability to problem-solve and think critically using systems-thinking. Proven track record of collaboration and exceptional customer service required. Preferred Qualifications CPP, CEBS, SHRM-CP/SCP, or other related certification. Familiarity with Workday payroll, absence, and time tracking. Knowledge of  Minnesota Paid Family and Medical Leave. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities Excellent written and interpersonal communication skills. Commitment to providing superior customer service. Strong problem-solving and critical thinking skills, and exceptional attention to detail and accuracy. Demonstrated ability to perform in a fast-paced, rapidly changing environment with multiple competing priorities. Strong attention to detail and accuracy. Able to take initiative, organize workflows, manage tasks and projects. Ability to work effectively and collaboratively in a diverse work environment. Ability to work effectively in a team environment and independently with little supervision. Excellent computer skills, ability to learn new systems. \n\n Application Requirements To be considered for this position please include the following in your application: Cover Letter (required). Resume (required). Compensation & Benefits at Augsburg The compensation is $70,000 - $78,000, DOQ.  Augsburg University offers a competitive and comprehensive total rewards program including: Medical, dental and vision coverage A generous 403(b) matching program with an employer contributions of up to 8% upon eligibility Up to 100% tuition remission for employees, spouses and dependents, and participation in the Tuition Exchange program with colleges and universities throughout the US Generous paid time-off, including 14 paid holidays, 12 sick days, 2 community service days, and vacation of up to 22 days per year immediately upon hire Employer-paid STD, LTD and life insurance Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for all employees Equal Opportunity Statement Augsburg is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color, or any other protected class.   Augsburg University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color, or any other protected class. If you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at phone number: 612-330-1058 or email: hr@augsburg.edu. \n\n Augsburg University has maintained a strong academic reputation defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies since 1869. A welcoming campus in the heart of Minneapolis, Augsburg offers undergraduate and graduate degrees to nearly 3,200 diverse students. Augsburg’s mission is to educate students to be informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, critical thinkers, and responsible leaders. The Augsburg experience is supported by an engaged community that is committed to intentional diversity in its life and work. An Augsburg education is defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies, guided by the faith and values of the Lutheran church, and shaped by its urban and global settings. Augsburg invites individuals who share our mission and commitment to intentional diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging to join our community.  In particular, Augsburg invites BIPOC, LGBTQIA+, individuals with disabilities, women, veterans and those from underrepresented or marginalized backgrounds are encouraged to apply.",
      "department": "Human Resources"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/AugsburgUniversity-MinneapolisMN/744000156860261": {
      "title": "MSW Field Director & Non-Tenure Track Faculty, Social Work",
      "description": "The Social Work Department at Augsburg University invites applications for a non-tenure track MSW Field Director position to begin January 2027. This is a full-time, 10-month, benefits-eligible three-year limited-term position.  The Augsburg Social Work Department is distinctive for its anti-oppressive and culturally responsive emphasis as well as deep-seated commitment to social justice and global issues. We value student-centered learning, emphasizing experiential learning strategies. We offer small class sizes and we leverage our strong community connections. MSW classes meet in-person two weekends per month and asynchronously on-line.  The MSW Field Director is responsible for the overall administration of the MSW field education program and teaching MSW courses. Duties include:  Departmental Representation to the Community Represents and promotes the MSW Field Program with existing and potential field sites Recruits, develops, approves and maintains field placements for MSW students in generalist, clinical, and macro field placements Represent Augsburg’s MSW programs at community events, outreach opportunities, and with the the Twin Cities MSW Field Consortium Coordinate orientation and continuing education for field agencies and field instructors Recruit external field instructors, as needed Field Program Management Assures maintenance and communication of database of field agencies, coordinates with the social work program coordinator and student workers as needed Assures delivery, maintenance, and archiving of all MSW student learning agendas in collaboration with staff Conduct evaluations of MSW Field program and maintains appropriate documentation; Matches and refers students to field placements Engages in problem-solving and decision-making around significant field placement difficulties in consultation with the MSW Program Director Implements MSW field policies and practices Consults and coordinates with the Department Chair, the MSW Program Director and the BSW Field Director to ensure consistent collaboration and integration of field programming and academic programs Develops and conducts field orientations for all MSW students Field Education Responsibilities within the Department Teach MSW courses, including field seminars Updates and maintains the MSW Field Manual Develops, implements, and maintains a field program consistent with accreditation standards of the Council of Social Work Education Adapt field learning agreements consistent with new accreditation standards Implements policies and procedures established by the Department for student field education Initiates consideration of new policies and procedures for maintaining and improving the quality of student field education Initiates expansion of field placement options using innovation and creativity to grow programs in conjunction with the Social Work Department Co-chairs the Field Committee of the Social Work Department Organizes internal departmental continuing education events Uphold standards of the profession including the NASW Code of Ethics and the Guidelines for Field Education as developed by the CSWE \n\n MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:  A Master’s of Social Work from a CSWE-accredited social work program is required A minimum of 3 years of direct social work practice experience A current graduate level social work license (LGSW, LICSW, or LISW), or eligibility for licensure in the state of Minnesota Ability to foster a positive and inclusive learning environment. Skills to navigate technological platforms for data collection, management and communication and hybrid and online learning pedagogies Excellent communication, organizational, and multi-tasking skills with proven ability to work collaboratively with internal and external stakeholders Strong interpersonal skills required to work with students, faculty, staff, other academic professionals and with community partners Demonstrated commitment to social work education, and familiarity with fulfilling the requirements of the Council on Social Work Education accreditation standards Ability to commit to the core attributes of the departmental mission, particularly in terms of our focus on anti-racist and anti-oppressive social work practice PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:  Teaching experience in higher education Experience serving as a MSW field instructor Experience in program development and/or administration Familiarity and experience with the Council on Social Work Education accreditation standards \n\n Compensation and Benefits The salary range for this position is $62,000 - $67,000, annually, depending on hiring rank and qualifications. Augsburg University offers a competitive and comprehensive benefits program, including:  Medical, dental and vision insurance coverage. Medical plans include Kavira direct care, which provides free or low-cost virtual and in-home primary care appointments and labs A generous 403(b) retirement program with an employer contribution of up to 8% upon eligibility Up to 100% tuition remission for employees, spouses and dependents, and participation in the Tuition Exchange program with colleges and universities throughout the US Employer-paid short-term disability, long-term disability, and life insurance Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for all employees Paid parental leave Application Instructions and Requirements To ensure full consideration, application materials should be received by November 15, 2026 . Position open until filled. To apply for this position, please upload the following documents: Cover letter: please address why you are interested in Augsburg University and this position, how your previous professional and academic experiences make you a strong candidate for this position, and how you believe you would contribute to and enhance the Augsburg Social Work Department Curriculum Vitae Unoffical MSW transcripts (official transcripts are required at time of hire) As part of the online application process, candidates are asked to provide the name, email address, and nature of professional relationship for three professional references. One of the references must be able to address your teaching or teaching potential. If your application advances in this search, you will be notified prior to Augsburg contacting your references.  If you have questions regarding the position, please contact the Search Chair: Erin Sugrue at sugrue@augsburg.edu.  Augsburg University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color, or any other protected class. If you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at phone number: 612-330-1058 or email: hr@augsburg.edu. \n\n Augsburg University  has maintained a strong academic reputation defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies since 1869. A welcoming campus in the heart of Minneapolis, Augsburg offers undergraduate and graduate degrees to nearly 3,200 diverse students. Augsburg’s mission is to educate students to be informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, critical thinkers, and responsible leaders. The Augsburg experience is supported by an engaged community that is committed to intentional diversity in its life and work. An Augsburg education is defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies, guided by the faith and values of the Lutheran church, and shaped by its urban and global settings. Augsburg invites individuals who share our mission and commitment to intentional diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging to join our community. Augsburg encourages BIPOC, LGBTQIA+, individuals with disabilities, women, veterans and those from underrepresented or marginalized backgrounds to apply.",
      "department": "Master of Social Work"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/AugsburgUniversity-MinneapolisMN/744000156085504": {
      "title": "Non-Tenure Track, Clinical Assistant Professor, Physician Associate Studies",
      "description": "The Physician Associate (PA) Studies Program at Augsburg University invites candidates to apply for a \nfull-time, non-tenure-track faculty position. This renewable 3-year special appointment blends clinical \nphase coordination with didactic teaching and program support. At least 0.5 full-time equivalent (FTE) of this 1.0 FTE appointment is dedicated to the clinical phase. In \nthis role, the faculty member works alongside the Director of Clinical Education (DCE) to develop and \nmaintain clinical sites with the clinical team, conduct site visits, advise and coach students through their clinical experiences, and assess student and site performance during the clinical phase. \nThe remaining effort supports the didactic phase and broader program needs. Depending on program \npriorities and the candidate's strengths, this may include classroom and skills instruction, accreditation compliance with the Accreditation Review Commission on Education for the Physician Assistant (ARC-PA) Standards, program assessment, and, for qualified candidates, teaching in the department's Doctor of Medical Science (DMSc) program. The successful candidate is a self-motivated team member looking to grow their own educational and \nprofessional experience, as well as the program's. This person will work well in collaboration with a cohesive and experienced group of faculty and professional staff. Responsibilities \n● Promote an inclusive learning environment \n● Serve as instructional leader for at least 9 course/instructional credits per semester across the \nclinical and didactic phases of the PA program, with additional DMSc credits as able or assigned \n● Participate in the ongoing PA program self-assessment, analysis, and accreditation process for \ncourses, instructional faculty, and program curriculum \n● Participate in curriculum development, teaching, and mapping according to ARC-PA Standards \nin both the didactic and clinical phases \n● Participate as a member of PA program committees and university-level committees \n● Participate in state and national PA organizations as necessary to promote the program and the \nprofession \n● Participate in the admissions process, including student recruitment and selection \n● Participate in professional development activities outside of Augsburg University's PA program \nin areas of clinical practice, scholarly activities, or advancement of educational degree, as agreed \nupon by the Program and School Directors, and provide an annual report of such activities per the \nAugsburg Faculty Handbook \n● Support and participate in the annual review of the PA program mission statement Clinical phase (at least 0.5 FTE), in support of the Director of Clinical Education (DCE) \n● Partner with the DCE and clinical staff on recruitment, development, and retention of preceptors \nand clinical sites \n● Conduct site visits and site assessments according to program policies and procedures and ARC- \nPA Standards \n● Advise, coach, and mentor students through their clinical experiences, including remediation as \nnecessary \n● Provide student instruction and assessment during the clinical phase, including data collection \nand evaluation, grading, and tracking of student progress \n● Help develop and maintain clinical phase learning objectives, outcomes, and student assessments, \nand organize hands-on learning experiences on call back days \n● Assist with development of tools to assess the effectiveness of the clinical curriculum and clinical \nsites \n● Maintain student data, assignments, and professionalism or discipline matters based on policies in \nthe Program Handbook \n● Maintain Continuing Medical Education (CME) certification status for PA preceptors Didactic phase and program support (remaining FTE) \n● Provide academic instruction in the faculty member's area of expertise, including lectures, \nphysical exam and technical skills instruction, and facilitation of small group and case-based \nlearning \n● Develop learning objectives, learning outcomes, and student assessments for assigned didactic \ncourses \n● Provide coaching, advising, remediation, and tutoring for students deficient in knowledge or \nskills as necessary \n● Support program assessment and accreditation compliance, including data collection and analysis \nand preparation of materials related to ARC-PA Standards \n● Assist with development of tools to assess the effectiveness of the didactic curriculum \n● For qualified candidates, teach, advise, or mentor students in the DMSc program as assigned by \nthe department \n\n Minimum qualifications \n● Master's degree in PA studies \n● Current certification by the National Commission on Certification of Physician Assistants \n(NCCPA) \n● Eligibility for PA licensure in Minnesota \n● Minimum of three (3) years of clinical experience as a PA \n● Previous in-person or virtual teaching experience within a PA educational program \n● Demonstrated organizational and professional skills \n● Proficiency in using spreadsheet software Preferred but not required qualifications \n● Doctoral degree (required for DMSc teaching assignments) \n● Experience in PA clinical education, such as precepting, clinical site development, or site visits \n● Experience with program assessment, curriculum mapping, or ARC-PA accreditation processes \n\n Compensation and Benefits \nThe salary range for this position is $95,000 - $100,000, annually, depending on hiring rank and qualifications. Augsburg University offers a competitive and comprehensive benefits program, including:  Medical, dental and vision insurance coverage. Medical plans include Kavira direct care, which provides free or low-cost virtual and in-home primary care appointments and labs A generous 403(b) retirement program with an employer contribution of up to 8% upon eligibility Up to 100% tuition remission for employees, spouses and dependents, and participation in the Tuition Exchange program with colleges and universities throughout the US Employer-paid short-term disability, long-term disability, and life insurance Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for all employees Paid parental leave Application Instructions and Requirements \nInitial review of application materials will begin on  November 2, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. To apply for this position, please upload the following documents: Cover letter: Please address why you are interested in Augsburg University and this position, how your previous professional and academic experiences make you a strong candidate for this position, and how you believe you would contribute to and enhance the Augsburg Physician Associate Studies Program Curriculum Vitae Copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts transcripts  Official transcripts will be required if hired. As part of the online application process, candidates are asked to provide the name, email address, and nature of professional relationship for three professional references. One of the references must be able to address your teaching or teaching potential. If your application advances in this search, you will be notified prior to Augsburg contacting your references.  If you have questions regarding the position, please contact the Search Chair: Danielle Skoglund at skogluda@augsburg.edu.  Augsburg University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color, or any other protected class. If you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at phone number: 612-330-1058 or email: hr@augsburg.edu. \n\n Augsburg University  has maintained a strong academic reputation defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies since 1869. A welcoming campus in the heart of Minneapolis, Augsburg offers undergraduate and graduate degrees to nearly 3,200 diverse students. Augsburg’s mission is to educate students to be informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, critical thinkers, and responsible leaders. The Augsburg experience is supported by an engaged community that is committed to intentional diversity in its life and work. An Augsburg education is defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies, guided by the faith and values of the Lutheran church, and shaped by its urban and global settings. Augsburg invites individuals who share our mission and commitment to intentional diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging to join our community. Augsburg encourages BIPOC, LGBTQIA+, individuals with disabilities, women, veterans and those from underrepresented or marginalized backgrounds to apply. About Augsburg PA \nEstablished in 1994, Augsburg PA is Minnesota's first PA program. Augsburg was also the first in the state to launch the Doctor of Medical Science degree for PAs and, in 2026, the first to formally adopt the national professional title of Physician Associate. The 27-month program includes 15 months of clinically integrated coursework followed by 12 months of supervised clinical rotations at sites across Minnesota, the Upper Midwest, and beyond. Students build practice-ready skills through case-based learning, projects, and hands-on training, including simulation and point of care ultrasound (POCUS). PA Program Mission \nThe Augsburg PA program is dedicated to educating compassionate, community-oriented, and forward-thinking health care professionals who are prepared to practice in primary care and address a wide range of patient needs. The program emphasizes team-based learning to prepare students for collaborative patient care, grounded in connection, respect, and innovation. The program's goal is to develop informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, and critical thinkers who are equipped to provide high-quality care across varied clinical and community settings.",
      "department": "Master of Physician Assistant Studies"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/AugsburgUniversity-MinneapolisMN/744000158364919": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Admissions Engagement ",
      "description": "Summary of Position  The Assistant Director of Admission Engagement curates the visit experience of our prospective undergraduate and graduate students. The assistant director will oversee all aspects of student visits, virtually and in person, including using the CRM to communicate effectively with prospective students, and providing detailed reporting on capacity and experience. This role oversees the student workers including hiring, training, scheduling, and supervising students. Primary Responsibilities Supervise, assess, and improve on-campus recruitment visitor services function which includes the administration of student employees and student tour guides as well as scheduling, training, and managing the Auggie Ambassadors including tour guides and phoners. Lead and assess our community engagement platform initiatives i.e ZeeMee Oversee the effectiveness for scheduling visits for walk-ins and develop/maintain the online visit data from Slate CRM. Utilize project management skills in event management for Enrollment Division. Coordinate the appropriate correspondence (visit confirmations, directions, etc.) with prospective students through multiple modes of response for both graduate and undergraduate market segments Lead the development and execution for group visits for new day, adult, graduate students including both transfers and or international students. Lead social media outreach for prospective student populations using our Admission platforms like Instagram, Twitter, Facebook, and Snapchat. Coordinate with Admissions leadership to maximize the Slate CRM program in the recruitment process, visit experience, acquire accurate data, define and develop excellent business practices, and assist in the development of helpful reporting. Coordinate with campus partners to target specific prospects throughout the year, providing academic departments and other key departments with consistent updates to ensure professionalism, accuracy, and superior customer service to all potential students and community college partners. Develop and maintain a Faculty engagement program. Provide superior customer service to students for the Admission staff for quality improvement of the student experience in the Admissions department as a whole. Additional Responsibilities Attend campus events to stay engaged with the student experience.   Attend trainings, as appropriate on customer service, student experience, and CRM management Coordinate office functions including ordering supplies and managing meetings All other duties as apparent or assigned by supervisor(s). Work Environment and Physical Demands Typical work environment is an office. Due to the nature of this role, a formal remote work arrangement is not feasible. Regional travel at various fairs which includes presenting.  Long or irregular work hours during seasonal needs Regular phone and computer use.  Occasional intense work environment as it relates to emotional reactions from students and/or parents Medium work - Exerting 20 to 50 pounds of force occasionally, and/or 10 to 25 pounds of force frequently, and/or greater than negligible up to 10 pounds of force constantly to move objects. \n\n Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Minimum four (4) years of professional experience in customer service. Experience in event planning or project management. Experience supervising or providing work direction to professional staff or student employees. Preferred Qualifications Experience using a CRM, Technolutions/Slate preferred Ability to speak bilingually: Spanish, Somali, Arabic or Hmong Professional experience in higher education Previous work experience in an admission office (as a student or in a professional capacity) Experience managing a budget Strong communications skills, including strong active listening; professional written communication skills; public speaking skills. Skilled at working with intergenerational colleagues and families Effective time management skills Team player, effective at collaboration Experience with Microsoft Suite of products (word, excel), Zoom, and Google Suite of products (word doc, sheets, google meet) Knowledge, Skills and Ability  Ability to work independently with little supervision. Ability to lead team meetings effectively. Ability and excitement to work effectively in a diverse work environment. \n\n Application Requirements To be considered for this position please include the following in your application: Resume (required). Compensation & Benefits at Augsburg The compensation is $48,000 - $52,000, DOQ. Augsburg University offers a competitive and comprehensive total rewards program including: Medical, dental and vision coverage A generous 403(b) matching program with an employer contributions of up to 8% upon eligibility Up to 100% tuition remission for employees, spouses and dependents, and participation in the Tuition Exchange program with colleges and universities throughout the US Generous paid time-off, including 14 paid holidays, 12 sick days, 2 community service days, and vacation of up to 22 days per year immediately upon hire Employer-paid STD, LTD and life insurance Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for all employees Equal Opportunity Statement Augsburg is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color, or any other protected class.   Augsburg University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of gender, sexual orientation, marital status, gender identity, race, age, disability, religion, national origin, color, or any other protected class. If you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact our Human Resources Department at phone number: 612-330-1058 or email: hr@augsburg.edu. \n\n Augsburg University has maintained a strong academic reputation defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies since 1869. A welcoming campus in the heart of Minneapolis, Augsburg offers undergraduate and graduate degrees to nearly 3,200 diverse students. Augsburg’s mission is to educate students to be informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, critical thinkers, and responsible leaders. The Augsburg experience is supported by an engaged community that is committed to intentional diversity in its life and work. An Augsburg education is defined by excellence in the liberal arts and professional studies, guided by the faith and values of the Lutheran church, and shaped by its urban and global settings. Augsburg invites individuals who share our mission and commitment to intentional diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging to join our community.  In particular, Augsburg invites BIPOC, LGBTQIA+, individuals with disabilities, women, veterans and those from underrepresented or marginalized backgrounds are encouraged to apply.",
      "department": "Admissions/Admissions Operations"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/AugsburgUniversity-MinneapolisMN/744000158569391": {
      "title": "Student: Philanthropy Ambassador, 2026-27",
      "description": "Are you passionate about Augsburg, relationships, and the power of generosity? We're looking \nfor a self-motivated student to serve as a Philanthropy Ambassador — a peer educator who \nhelps fellow students understand how donor support shapes their Augsburg experience. Duties: Learn how donor-funded scholarships directly reduce tuition and make an Augsburg education more accessible Engage fellow students in meaningful conversations about the culture of giving and its impact on our community Facilitate connections between students and their scholarship benefactors through thank-you outreach Represent the values of generosity, gratitude, and relationship-building across campus Position Details This is a paid annual position working with the Advancement Team and requires approximately \n12 hours per month. \n\n Who We're Looking For \nYou're an Augsburg enthusiast — someone who genuinely loves this university and wants to \nchampion what makes it special. You're a strong communicator who believes relationships are \nthe foundation of a healthier society. You take initiative, work independently, and are curious \nabout how generosity creates opportunity for students and communities alike. \nThis role is a great fit if you: Are proud to be an Auggies and love sharing that pride with others Value authentic connection and community Are comfortable starting conversations and influencing peers Want to make your time at Augsburg meaningful beyond the classroom \n\n All student applicants must attach the following for consideration:  Resume Cover Letter (optional) Augsburg University is an Equal Opportunity employer.  We are committed to providing equal employment opportunity to all applicants and employees regardless of their race, creed, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability, military service, protected veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity, transgender status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. \nIf you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact the Human Resources department by phone at  612.330.1058 or email at hr@augsburg.edu.  Human Resources is located at 20 Memorial Hall. \n\n Augsburg University is committed to helping our student explore their vocation. As a University with a calling, we welcome the unique gifts that each of our employees brings to our collective work, and we are committed to supporting our students as they seek to match those gifts with the needs of the University and our larger community.    Student employment with Augsburg is more than a job - it is an opportunity for Augsburg students to gain meaningful work experience in a supportive setting that promotes professional growth, personal accountability, teamwork and collaboration and quality work that lives up to our mission of educating students to be informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, critical thinkers, and responsible leaders.",
      "department": "Advancement Services"
    }
  },
